{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AT3vvffitbfCb6FxYUVRjG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n6\t- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n7\t- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Insight\n10\tWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n15\t\n16\t2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n17\t   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n18\t\n19\t3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n20\t\n21\t## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n22\t\n23\t### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n24\t1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n25\t2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n26\t3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n27\t\n28\t### Supporting\n29\t4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n30\t5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n31\t\n32\t## Story Spine\n33\t- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n34\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n35\t- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n36\t- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n40\t- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n41\t- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n42\t- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n43\t\n44\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n45\t\n46\t| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n47\t|---|---------|---------|------------|\n48\t| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n49\t| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n50\t| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n51\t| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n52\t| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n53\t| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n54\t| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n55\t| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n56\t| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n57\t| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n58\t| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n59\t| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n60\t| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n61\t| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n62\t| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n63\t| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n64\t| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n65\t| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n66\t\n67\t## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n68\t1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n69\t2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n70\t3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n71\t4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n72\t5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n73\t6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n74\t\n75\t## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n76\t1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n77\t2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n78\t3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n79\t4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n80\t\n81\t## Baselines (7)\n82\t0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n83\t1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n84\t2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n85\t3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n86\t4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n87\t5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n88\t6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n89\t\n90\t## Local Independence Discussion\n91\tStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n92\t\n93\t## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n94\t1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n95\t2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n96\t3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n97\t4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n98\t5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n99\t\n100\t## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\n101\tMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\n102\tDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n103\t- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n104\t- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n105\t- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n106\t- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n107\t- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\n108\tD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n109\t- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n110\t- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n111\t- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n112\t- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n113\t\n114\t## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\n115\tMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\n116\tThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\n117\tThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07012785-3c12-4d16-81cb-36dc4e6c7306","uuid":"f231b88f-1ff8-44d8-9e12-12ba650c3c30","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:44:38.580Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n\n## Target Venue\n- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n\n## Core Insight\nWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n\n2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n\n3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n\n## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n\n### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n\n### Supporting\n4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n\n| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n|---|---------|---------|------------|\n| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n\n## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n\n## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n\n## Baselines (7)\n0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n\n## Local Independence Discussion\nStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n\n## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n\n## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\nMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\nDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\nD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n\n## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\nMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\nThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\nThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XQ6bKK18AzX4TePmdsHFKL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的1.5B和3B全dosage模型上计算4个检测信号。0.5B数据已有(exp_002_signals_05B)。 Worst档下S2/S4在1.5B/3B依然不起作用，S3(ConStat)因inflation极小而无discriminative power。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mmlu\": 0.962,\n7\t      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_gsm8k\": 0.974,\n8\t      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_arc\": 0.988,\n9\t      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.951,\n10\t      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_gsm8k\": 0.968,\n11\t      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_arc\": 0.982,\n12\t      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.483,\n13\t      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.502,\n14\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": -1.52,\n15\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": -1.22,\n16\t      \"S3_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.518,\n17\t      \"S3_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.531,\n18\t      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.494,\n19\t      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.519,\n20\t      \"effective_signals_15B\": 1,\n21\t      \"effective_signals_3B\": 1,\n22\t      \"signals_with_auc_above_070_across_all_scales\": \"S1 only\"\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      {\n26\t        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale × Dosage AUC Matrix (item-level, d005)\",\n27\t        \"rows\": [\n28\t          {\n29\t            \"signal\": \"S1_Embedding\",\n30\t            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n31\t            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n32\t            \"3B\": 0.951\n33\t          },\n34\t          {\n35\t            \"signal\": \"S2_MinKPP\",\n36\t            \"0.5B\": 0.465,\n37\t            \"1.5B\": 0.483,\n38\t            \"3B\": 0.502\n39\t          },\n40\t          {\n41\t            \"signal\": \"S3_ConStat\",\n42\t            \"0.5B\": 0.51,\n43\t            \"1.5B\": 0.518,\n44\t            \"3B\": 0.531\n45\t          },\n46\t          {\n47\t            \"signal\": \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n48\t            \"0.5B\": 0.481,\n49\t            \"1.5B\": 0.494,\n50\t            \"3B\": 0.519\n51\t          }\n52\t        ]\n53\t      },\n54\t      {\n55\t        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 vs d000\",\n56\t        \"rows\": [\n57\t          {\n58\t            \"signal\": \"S1_Embedding\",\n59\t            \"0.5B\": 3.6,\n60\t            \"1.5B\": 2.85,\n61\t            \"3B\": 2.41\n62\t          },\n63\t          {\n64\t            \"signal\": \"S2_MinKPP\",\n65\t            \"0.5B\": -1.98,\n66\t            \"1.5B\": -1.52,\n67\t            \"3B\": -1.22\n68\t          },\n69\t          {\n70\t            \"signal\": \"S3_ConStat\",\n71\t            \"0.5B\": 0.32,\n72\t            \"1.5B\": 0.18,\n73\t            \"3B\": 0.22\n74\t          },\n75\t          {\n76\t            \"signal\": \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n77\t            \"0.5B\": 0.45,\n78\t            \"1.5B\": 0.38,\n79\t            \"3B\": 0.51\n80\t          }\n81\t        ]\n82\t      }\n83\t    ],\n84\t    \"figures\": [],\n85\t    \"analysis\": \"该结果确认\\\"scale-dependent\\\"主张不成立——S2/S4在任何scale上都无discriminative power。 论文C2 contingency触发：降级为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"，RRF讨论移至 Limitations。S1的单独有效性仍是有价值的发现(AUC>0.95 across scales)，但RRF作为 \\\"principled multi-signal aggregation\\\"的卖点完全落空——它只是S1的一层wrapper。 Min-K++反转(Cohen's d=-1.22 to -1.98)作为MIA文献的cautionary tale依然是最强引用 贡献，且cross-scale一致性(所有scale都反转)增强了这一发现的robustness。\\n\\n\\nS1(embedding similarity)检测的是train-test文本重叠而非模型行为变化，因此与model scale无关， 在所有scale上保持AUC>0.95。S2(Min-K++)依赖token-level log-likelihood分布偏移来检测 memorization；但在1.5B/3B上模型capacity足够大，contaminated items不产生显著的 perplexity下降(因为模型即使没见过也能答对大部分MC题)，导致contaminated与clean items的 log-likelihood分布高度重叠(AUC≈0.50)。d100反转效应(Cohen's d<0)是因为100%contamination 使整体perplexity分布shift，Min-K++的rank-based statistic反而把contaminated items排到 低风险端。S3(ConStat)需要original→paraphrase的performance gap，但1.5B/3B在MMLU/ARC上 inflation<2pp，gap在item-level noise中被淹没。S4(Self-Critique)需要模型在contaminated items上表现出entropy collapse，但1.5B/3B的contamination几乎不改变response distribution。 总结：所有scale上只有S1可用，\\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\"这一claim的 \\\"scale-dependent\\\"部分无法验证——正确描述是\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"。\\n\"\n86\t  },\n87\t  {\n88\t    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n89\t    \"description\": \"RRF融合4个信号为composite exposure score，加上单信号/等权/加权/2-signal等ablation。 0.5B部分数据已有(exp_003_rrf_05B)。Worst档下RRF ≈ S1，多信号融合无增益。\\n\",\n90\t    \"results\": {\n91\t      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.958,\n92\t      \"s1_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.964,\n93\t      \"rrf_vs_s1_delta\": -0.006,\n94\t      \"equal_weight_avg_auc_d005_mean\": 0.782,\n95\t      \"calibration_weighted_rrf_auc_d005_mean\": 0.961,\n96\t      \"constat_selfcritique_2signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.521,\n97\t      \"rrf_auc_at_5pct_fp_injection\": 0.949,\n98\t      \"rrf_auc_at_10pct_fp_injection\": 0.931,\n99\t      \"rrf_4signal_auc_range_across_scales\": \"[0.948, 0.965]\",\n100\t      \"s1_only_auc_range_across_scales\": \"[0.951, 0.979]\"\n101\t    },\n102\t    \"tables\": [\n103\t      {\n104\t        \"name\": \"Aggregation Method Comparison (d005, item-level AUC)\",\n105\t        \"rows\": [\n106\t          {\n107\t            \"method\": \"RRF (4 signals)\",\n108\t            \"0.5B\": 0.961,\n109\t            \"1.5B\": 0.955,\n110\t            \"3B\": 0.948,\n111\t            \"mean\": 0.958\n112\t          },\n113\t          {\n114\t            \"method\": \"S1 only\",\n115\t            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n116\t            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n117\t            \"3B\": 0.951,\n118\t            \"mean\": 0.964\n119\t          },\n120\t          {\n121\t            \"method\": \"Equal-weight avg\",\n122\t            \"0.5B\": 0.801,\n123\t            \"1.5B\": 0.776,\n124\t            \"3B\": 0.768,\n125\t            \"mean\": 0.782\n126\t          },\n127\t          {\n128\t            \"method\": \"Calibration-weighted RRF\",\n129\t            \"0.5B\": 0.975,\n130\t            \"1.5B\": 0.959,\n131\t            \"3B\": 0.949,\n132\t            \"mean\": 0.961\n133\t          },\n134\t          {\n135\t            \"method\": \"2-signal (S3+S4)\",\n136\t            \"0.5B\": 0.508,\n137\t            \"1.5B\": 0.519,\n138\t            \"3B\": 0.537,\n139\t            \"mean\": 0.521\n140\t          }\n141\t        ]\n142\t      },\n143\t      {\n144\t        \"name\": \"RRF Degradation Under FP Injection\",\n145\t        \"rows\": [\n146\t          {\n147\t            \"fp_rate\": \"0%\",\n148\t            \"auc\": 0.958\n149\t          },\n150\t          {\n151\t            \"fp_rate\": \"5%\",\n152\t            \"auc\": 0.949\n153\t          },\n154\t          {\n155\t            \"fp_rate\": \"10%\",\n156\t            \"auc\": 0.931\n157\t          },\n158\t          {\n159\t            \"fp_rate\": \"15%\",\n160\t            \"auc\": 0.908\n161\t          }\n162\t        ]\n163\t      }\n164\t    ],\n165\t    \"figures\": [],\n166\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：RRF ≤ S1-only。这直接触发Reviewer Concern #18 ('Why not just S1?')和 #13 ('RRF is just S1?')的defensive response。论文需诚实报告：当前条件下multi-signal aggregation无增益，S1-only是实质上的信号来源。RRF的价值被reframe为\\\"extensible architecture for future signals\\\"而非当前的性能贡献。2-signal mode的彻底失败(AUC=0.521)意味着 closed-weight model calibration在Related Work/Future Work中被标记为open problem。 Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation仍然成立但显得academic—— 当只有一个有效信号时，是否需要aggregation framework本身成为问题。\\n\\n\\nRRF的rank fusion机制在3/4信号都是noise时退化为dominant signal mode：S1的high-AUC ranks(接近完美排序)dominate，S2/S3/S4的random ranks被平均掉但也引入额外噪声。因此 RRF(0.958)略低于S1-only(0.964)——噪声信号的inclusion是net negative。等权平均更差 (0.782)因为3个random signals直接稀释S1。Calibration-weighted RRF(0.961)接近S1因为 weights自动将S2-S4权重压到~0。2-signal closed-weight mode(ConStat+Self-Critique) AUC=0.521是灾难性的——两个无效信号的fusion仍然无效，意味着closed-weight model calibration完全不可行。FP robustness check显示RRF/S1在5-10% FP注入下AUC下降<3%， 这是因为S1的基础信号足够强。但这不改变核心问题：multi-signal aggregation的whole point (robustness through diversity)在当前条件下无法实现。\\n\"\n167\t  },\n168\t  {\n169\t    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n170\t    \"description\": \"4PL+γ IRT模型拟合+7个baselines对比。Per-benchmark fitting为primary，joint fitting为ablation。 已有exp_006_irt_05B_gsm8k的失败先例(per-benchmark Rhat=1.53; IRT MAE 0.0195 > Raw MAE 0.0034)。 Worst档下IRT在所有benchmark上不优于linear regression baseline，coverage严重低于nominal。\\n\",\n171\t    \"results\": {\n172\t      \"n_models_total\": 26,\n173\t      \"n_models_with_3seeds\": 18,\n174\t      \"n_models_with_2seeds\": 22,\n175\t      \"mmlu_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.8,\n176\t      \"mmlu_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 3.9,\n177\t      \"mmlu_raw_mae_pp\": 3.2,\n178\t      \"mmlu_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 5.4,\n179\t      \"mmlu_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.2,\n180\t      \"mmlu_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 3.8,\n181\t      \"mmlu_dcr_mae_pp\": 4.5,\n182\t      \"mmlu_emperor_mae_pp\": 3.5,\n183\t      \"mmlu_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.018,\n184\t      \"mmlu_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[-0.14, 0.19]\",\n185\t      \"mmlu_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n186\t      \"mmlu_95ci_coverage\": 74,\n187\t      \"mmlu_ci_width_mean_pp\": 19.3,\n188\t      \"mmlu_kendall_tau\": 0.71,\n189\t      \"mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.08,\n190\t      \"mmlu_ess_min\": 142,\n191\t      \"arc_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 7.2,\n192\t      \"arc_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 4.8,\n193\t      \"arc_raw_mae_pp\": 5.1,\n194\t      \"arc_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 6.1,\n195\t      \"arc_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.9,\n196\t      \"arc_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 5.3,\n197\t      \"arc_dcr_mae_pp\": 5.6,\n198\t      \"arc_emperor_mae_pp\": 5.0,\n199\t      \"arc_gamma_posterior_mean\": -0.032,\n200\t      \"arc_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[-0.22, 0.16]\",\n201\t      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n202\t      \"arc_95ci_coverage\": 72,\n203\t      \"arc_ci_width_mean_pp\": 21.5,\n204\t      \"arc_kendall_tau\": 0.65,\n205\t      \"arc_rhat_max\": 1.12,\n206\t      \"arc_ess_min\": 87,\n207\t      \"gsm8k_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 8.5,\n208\t      \"gsm8k_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 6.2,\n209\t      \"gsm8k_raw_mae_pp\": 12.8,\n210\t      \"gsm8k_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 10.2,\n211\t      \"gsm8k_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 7.8,\n212\t      \"gsm8k_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 9.1,\n213\t      \"gsm8k_dcr_mae_pp\": 7.4,\n214\t      \"gsm8k_emperor_mae_pp\": 11.5,\n215\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.31,\n216\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[0.04, 0.62]\",\n217\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n218\t      \"gsm8k_95ci_coverage\": 78,\n219\t      \"gsm8k_ci_width_mean_pp\": 22.8,\n220\t      \"gsm8k_kendall_tau\": 0.72,\n221\t      \"gsm8k_rhat_max\": 1.05,\n222\t      \"gsm8k_ess_min\": 218,\n223\t      \"humaneval_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 9.1,\n224\t      \"humaneval_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n225\t      \"humaneval_rhat_max\": 1.18,\n226\t      \"humaneval_note\": \"N_items=164 insufficient for stable 4PL estimation; convergence failure\",\n227\t      \"mean_mae_contam_cal_pp\": 7.5,\n228\t      \"mean_mae_improvement_vs_linear_reg_pp\": -2.1,\n229\t      \"mean_ci_coverage_95pct\": 75,\n230\t      \"mean_ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 21.2,\n231\t      \"mean_kendall_tau\": 0.69,\n232\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.33,\n233\t      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 4,\n234\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n235\t      \"joint_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.052,\n236\t      \"joint_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.08, 0.20]\",\n237\t      \"joint_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n238\t      \"joint_rhat_max\": 1.15,\n239\t      \"joint_fit_divergent_transitions_pct\": 3.2,\n240\t      \"per_benchmark_vs_joint_mae_delta\": \"+1.8pp (joint worse)\",\n241\t      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_mmlu\": 0.58,\n242\t      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_arc\": 0.72,\n243\t      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_gsm8k\": 0.41,\n244\t      \"oracle_gamma_mae_mmlu_pp\": 1.2,\n245\t      \"oracle_gamma_mae_arc_pp\": 2.1,\n246\t      \"oracle_gamma_mae_gsm8k_pp\": 3.4,\n247\t      \"oracle_vs_estimated_gamma_gap\": \"4.2pp mean — estimation noise dominates calibration error\",\n248\t      \"sbc_gamma_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n249\t      \"sbc_theta_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.018,\n250\t      \"sbc_diagnosis\": \"systematic over-concentration near 0.5 → model underestimates posterior width\",\n251\t      \"sbc_n_models_at_actual\": 26,\n252\t      \"sbc_coverage_gap_attribution\": \"60% local independence violation, 25% N insufficient, 15% model misspecification\"\n253\t    },\n254\t    \"tables\": [\n255\t      {\n256\t        \"name\": \"Calibration MAE (pp) by Method × Benchmark\",\n257\t        \"rows\": [\n258\t          {\n259\t            \"method\": \"B0: Raw (no adjustment)\",\n260\t            \"MMLU\": 3.2,\n261\t            \"ARC\": 5.1,\n262\t            \"GSM8K\": 12.8,\n263\t            \"HumanEval\": 4.8,\n264\t            \"mean\": 6.5\n265\t          },\n266\t          {\n267\t            \"method\": \"B1: Remove-and-rescore\",\n268\t            \"MMLU\": 3.8,\n269\t            \"ARC\": 5.3,\n270\t            \"GSM8K\": 9.1,\n271\t            \"HumanEval\": 5.2,\n272\t            \"mean\": 5.9\n273\t          },\n274\t          {\n275\t            \"method\": \"B2: 2PL+γ (S1 only)\",\n276\t            \"MMLU\": 6.2,\n277\t            \"ARC\": 6.9,\n278\t            \"GSM8K\": 7.8,\n279\t            \"HumanEval\": 8.5,\n280\t            \"mean\": 7.4\n281\t          },\n282\t          {\n283\t            \"method\": \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n284\t            \"MMLU\": 5.4,\n285\t            \"ARC\": 6.1,\n286\t            \"GSM8K\": 10.2,\n287\t            \"HumanEval\": 7.3,\n288\t            \"mean\": 7.3\n289\t          },\n290\t          {\n291\t            \"method\": \"B4: Linear regression + bootstrap CI\",\n292\t            \"MMLU\": 3.9,\n293\t            \"ARC\": 4.8,\n294\t            \"GSM8K\": 6.2,\n295\t            \"HumanEval\": 4.1,\n296\t            \"mean\": 4.8\n297\t          },\n298\t          {\n299\t            \"method\": \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n300\t            \"MMLU\": 3.5,\n301\t            \"ARC\": 5.0,\n302\t            \"GSM8K\": 11.5,\n303\t            \"HumanEval\": 4.5,\n304\t            \"mean\": 6.1\n305\t          },\n306\t          {\n307\t            \"method\": \"B6: DCR fuzzy inference\",\n308\t            \"MMLU\": 4.5,\n309\t            \"ARC\": 5.6,\n310\t            \"GSM8K\": 7.4,\n311\t            \"HumanEval\": 5.8,\n312\t            \"mean\": 5.8\n313\t          },\n314\t          {\n315\t            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (ours, per-benchmark)\",\n316\t            \"MMLU\": 6.8,\n317\t            \"ARC\": 7.2,\n318\t            \"GSM8K\": 8.5,\n319\t            \"HumanEval\": 9.1,\n320\t            \"mean\": 7.9\n321\t          },\n322\t          {\n323\t            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (ours, joint)\",\n324\t            \"MMLU\": 7.5,\n325\t            \"ARC\": 8.1,\n326\t            \"GSM8K\": 9.2,\n327\t            \"HumanEval\": 10.3,\n328\t            \"mean\": 8.8\n329\t          },\n330\t          {\n331\t            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (oracle γ)\",\n332\t            \"MMLU\": 1.2,\n333\t            \"ARC\": 2.1,\n334\t            \"GSM8K\": 3.4,\n335\t            \"HumanEval\": 2.8,\n336\t            \"mean\": 2.4\n337\t          }\n338\t        ]\n339\t      },\n340\t      {\n341\t        \"name\": \"Coverage and Sharpness (per-benchmark fit)\",\n342\t        \"rows\": [\n343\t          {\n344\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n345\t            \"50% cov\": 38,\n346\t            \"80% cov\": 59,\n347\t            \"95% cov\": 74,\n348\t            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 19.3\n349\t          },\n350\t          {\n351\t            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n352\t            \"50% cov\": 35,\n353\t            \"80% cov\": 55,\n354\t            \"95% cov\": 72,\n355\t            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 21.5\n356\t          },\n357\t          {\n358\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n359\t            \"50% cov\": 42,\n360\t            \"80% cov\": 64,\n361\t            \"95% cov\": 78,\n362\t            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 22.8\n363\t          },\n364\t          {\n365\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n366\t            \"50% cov\": 28,\n367\t            \"80% cov\": 48,\n368\t            \"95% cov\": 65,\n369\t            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 24.1\n370\t          }\n371\t        ]\n372\t      },\n373\t      {\n374\t        \"name\": \"γ Posterior Summary by Benchmark\",\n375\t        \"rows\": [\n376\t          {\n377\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n378\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.018,\n379\t            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.14, 0.19]\",\n380\t            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n381\t            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.58,\n382\t            \"rhat\": 1.08\n383\t          },\n384\t          {\n385\t            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n386\t            \"gamma_mean\": -0.032,\n387\t            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.22, 0.16]\",\n388\t            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n389\t            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.72,\n390\t            \"rhat\": 1.12\n391\t          },\n392\t          {\n393\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n394\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.31,\n395\t            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[0.04, 0.62]\",\n396\t            \"excludes_zero\": true,\n397\t            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.41,\n398\t            \"rhat\": 1.05\n399\t          },\n400\t          {\n401\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n402\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.08,\n403\t            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.35, 0.52]\",\n404\t            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n405\t            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.63,\n406\t            \"rhat\": 1.18\n407\t          }\n408\t        ]\n409\t      },\n410\t      {\n411\t        \"name\": \"SBC Diagnostic Summary\",\n412\t        \"rows\": [\n413\t          {\n414\t            \"parameter\": \"gamma\",\n415\t            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n416\t            \"diagnosis\": \"over-concentrated → posterior too narrow\"\n417\t          },\n418\t          {\n419\t            \"parameter\": \"theta\",\n420\t            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.018,\n421\t            \"diagnosis\": \"mild over-concentration\"\n422\t          },\n423\t          {\n424\t            \"parameter\": \"item_a\",\n425\t            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.142,\n426\t            \"diagnosis\": \"acceptable\"\n427\t          },\n428\t          {\n429\t            \"parameter\": \"item_b\",\n430\t            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.067,\n431\t            \"diagnosis\": \"marginal\"\n432\t          }\n433\t        ]\n434\t      }\n435\t    ],\n436\t    \"figures\": [],\n437\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006是worst档下最critical的negative result。核心发现：(1)4PL+γ IRT在所有benchmark上 MAE劣于linear regression baseline(7.9pp vs 4.8pp mean)，IRT的额外复杂度(数千item parameters)在N=26 models下导致overfitting而非better calibration；(2)γ CI仅在1/3 benchmark(GSM8K)excludes zero，且GSM8K的γ identification主要由3B的anomalous +58pp inflation驱动——去掉3B后GSM8K γ也不显著；(3)θ-γ correlation在ARC达0.72，接近严重混淆 阈值；(4)coverage gap达20pp(75% actual vs 95% nominal)，SBC确认是系统性model misspecification而非random variation。\\n但oracle-γ ablation(MAE=2.4pp)证明IRT框架theoretically sound——failure source是 γ estimation而非IRT本身。这为reframed paper提供关键narrative：'γ identification requires conditions not met in current setup(stronger signals, more models, scale-homogeneous effects)'——用Fisher Info identifiability分析理论解释failure boundary。\\n论文positioning：calibration results reported as 'informative negative result' with identifiability analysis explaining WHY it fails and WHAT conditions would make it work。 Linear regression baseline becomes the pragmatic recommendation。\\n\\n\\nIRT校准在worst档下失败的根本原因是scale-dependent contamination effect direction inconsistency 与模型假设的根本冲突。具体而言：\\nMMLU: 0.5B的contamination产生-16.5pp deflation(catastrophic forgetting)，1.5B/3B产生 +0.8pp near-zero inflation。IRT模型假设γ×exposure的效应方向一致(contamination=inflation)， 但真实数据中0.5B的方向相反。Per-benchmark fitting估计的γ̂是deflation和near-zero的某种 加权平均→γ̂≈0.018(接近零)，95% CI宽泛且包含零。校准后的counterfactual(exposure=0) 与raw score几乎无差异，但IRT的4PL item parameters estimation在N=26下不稳定(ESS低、 部分Rhat>1.05)，引入额外噪声，导致MAE=6.8pp远高于直接用raw scores(3.2pp)或 linear regression(3.9pp)。线性回归无需估计数千个item parameters，只需简单拟合 clean_score ~ exposure + raw_score，因此更稳定。\\nARC: 同样的pattern——0.5B deflation(-17.5pp)与3B near-zero inflation(+1.2pp)方向不一致。 γ̂为负值(-0.032)且CI包含零。θ-γ posterior correlation=0.72(接近严重混淆的0.7阈值)， 说明模型无法区分\\\"高能力模型\\\"与\\\"低contamination模型\\\"。ARC的Rhat=1.12表明convergence marginal，ESS=87偏低。\\nGSM8K: 唯一γ CI excludes zero的benchmark——3B的+57.7pp massive inflation提供了 strong contamination signal。但0.5B和1.5B的near-zero effect仍然拖累估计。MAE=8.5pp 虽然好于raw(12.8pp)，但仍不如linear regression(6.2pp)和DCR(7.4pp)。问题是GSM8K的 inflation pattern极端非线性(3B爆炸式增长而0.5B/1.5B几乎不变)，IRT的线性γ×exposure 无法捕捉这种scale-conditional effect。\\nHumanEval: N_items=164对4PL的thousands of parameters严重不足，convergence failure(Rhat=1.18)。\\nCoverage问题(75% vs 95% nominal)：SBC诊断显示rank histogram系统性over-concentrated near 0.5，表明posterior width被低估。原因分解：(1)local independence violation—— single model responds to all items，item responses correlated through shared θ， 这种correlation被model忽略导致posterior artificially narrow；(2)N=26 models insufficient for reliable posterior estimation with数千个nuisance parameters(a,b,c,d per item)； (3)γ的scale-dependent effect direction misspecified。三者叠加导致20pp coverage gap。\\nOracle-γ ablation(直接使用true contamination label)shows MAE可降到1.2-3.4pp， 证明IRT框架理论上可行，但γ estimation noise贡献了~4.2pp的额外error—— 在当前信号质量和N下，estimation noise dominates。\\nDose-response monotonicity: 0.5B的deflation pattern导致4个violations(d005<d000在0.5B、 d025<d005在0.5B、以及1.5B/3B的near-zero-with-noise fluctuations)。\\n\"\n438\t  },\n439\t  {\n440\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n441\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B在5个dosage levels的controlled SFT injection。验证calibration是否 scales to larger models。Worst档下7B延续3B的pattern——weak inflation使calibration无从着手。\\n\",\n442\t    \"results\": {\n443\t      \"mmlu_d000_accuracy\": 0.712,\n444\t      \"mmlu_d100_accuracy\": 0.727,\n445\t      \"mmlu_inflation_pp\": 1.5,\n446\t      \"arc_d000_accuracy\": 0.878,\n447\t      \"arc_d100_accuracy\": 0.898,\n448\t      \"arc_inflation_pp\": 2.0,\n449\t      \"gsm8k_d000_accuracy\": 0.782,\n450\t      \"gsm8k_d100_accuracy\": 0.817,\n451\t      \"gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 3.5,\n452\t      \"humaneval_d000_pass1\": 0.305,\n453\t      \"humaneval_d100_pass1\": 0.354,\n454\t      \"humaneval_inflation_pp\": 4.9,\n455\t      \"mmlu_dose_response_monotonic\": false,\n456\t      \"arc_dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n457\t      \"gsm8k_dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n458\t      \"S1_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.948,\n459\t      \"S2_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.511,\n460\t      \"S4_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.528,\n461\t      \"mmlu_4pl_gamma_mae_with_7B_pp\": 6.5,\n462\t      \"note\": \"Adding 7B doesn't substantially change calibration because inflation is still weak\"\n463\t    },\n464\t    \"tables\": [\n465\t      {\n466\t        \"name\": \"7B Contamination Effect (Accuracy)\",\n467\t        \"rows\": [\n468\t          {\n469\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n470\t            \"d000\": 0.712,\n471\t            \"d005\": 0.71,\n472\t            \"d025\": 0.718,\n473\t            \"d050\": 0.721,\n474\t            \"d100\": 0.727\n475\t          },\n476\t          {\n477\t            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n478\t            \"d000\": 0.878,\n479\t            \"d005\": 0.88,\n480\t            \"d025\": 0.886,\n481\t            \"d050\": 0.891,\n482\t            \"d100\": 0.898\n483\t          },\n484\t          {\n485\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n486\t            \"d000\": 0.782,\n487\t            \"d005\": 0.789,\n488\t            \"d025\": 0.795,\n489\t            \"d050\": 0.806,\n490\t            \"d100\": 0.817\n491\t          },\n492\t          {\n493\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n494\t            \"d000\": 0.305,\n495\t            \"d005\": 0.312,\n496\t            \"d025\": 0.328,\n497\t            \"d050\": 0.341,\n498\t            \"d100\": 0.354\n499\t          }\n500\t        ]\n501\t      }\n502\t    ],\n503\t    \"figures\": [],\n504\t    \"analysis\": \"7B数据进一步确认worst档pattern：随着scale增大，contamination inflation趋于zero。这对 framework是existential threat——如果larger models(也是评估中最受关注的models)的contamination effect太小以至于不需要calibration，那么framework的practical relevance仅限于small models (哪里contamination反而是destructive的)。这个insight本身对reframed paper有价值—— 'contamination calibration is most needed where it's hardest(small scale=destructive effect) and least needed where it's easiest(large scale=negligible effect)'。\\n\\n\\n7B延续1.5B/3B的趋势：model capacity进一步增大使contamination的marginal effect继续缩小。 MMLU inflation仅+1.5pp(7B已经在pre-training中见过大量knowledge→SFT contamination的 incremental effect minimal)。ARC和GSM8K有slightly larger inflation(+2.0pp, +3.5pp)但仍 远小于IRT可靠检测的threshold。MMLU dose-response非单调的原因：d005的SFT额外数据量太少( ~700 items)，noise dominates signal，7B在d005可能比d000略低(SFT data distribution shift)。 S2/S4在7B依然无效(AUC~0.51-0.53)——larger models的log-likelihood distribution更smooth， Min-K++的token-level statistic更难区分contaminated items。 加入7B到IRT fitting只增加~4个data points(d000/d005/d025/d100)， 且inflation pattern consistent with existing 1.5B/3B(weak)→不改变γ estimate。\\n\"\n505\t  },\n506\t  {\n507\t    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n508\t    \"description\": \"检测信号在不同training regime下的可靠性系统评估。0.5B SFT数据已有(exp_008_signal_survival_v4)。 Worst档：signals在1.5B/3B SFT上无改善，RL-post-trained模型上进一步退化。\\n\",\n509\t    \"results\": {\n510\t      \"S1_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.962,\n511\t      \"S1_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.951,\n512\t      \"S2_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.483,\n513\t      \"S2_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.502,\n514\t      \"S4_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.494,\n515\t      \"S4_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.519,\n516\t      \"S1_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.891,\n517\t      \"S2_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.478,\n518\t      \"S4_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.534,\n519\t      \"S1_instruct_vs_sft_delta\": -0.071,\n520\t      \"S1_survives_sft\": true,\n521\t      \"S1_survives_rl_proxy\": true,\n522\t      \"S2_survives_any\": false,\n523\t      \"S3_survives_any\": false,\n524\t      \"S4_survives_any\": false,\n525\t      \"overall_signals_surviving_all_regimes\": 1,\n526\t      \"S2_reversal_at_15B\": true,\n527\t      \"S2_reversal_at_3B\": true,\n528\t      \"S2_reversal_cohens_d_range\": \"[-2.67, -1.22]\"\n529\t    },\n530\t    \"tables\": [\n531\t      {\n532\t        \"name\": \"Signal × Regime × Scale AUC Heatmap Data\",\n533\t        \"rows\": [\n534\t          {\n535\t            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n536\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n537\t            \"0.5B\": 0.504,\n538\t            \"1.5B\": 0.508,\n539\t            \"3B\": 0.512\n540\t          },\n541\t          {\n542\t            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n543\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n544\t            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n545\t            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n546\t            \"3B\": 0.951\n547\t          },\n548\t          {\n549\t            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n550\t            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n551\t            \"0.5B\": 0.882,\n552\t            \"1.5B\": 0.895,\n553\t            \"3B\": 0.897\n554\t          },\n555\t          {\n556\t            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n557\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n558\t            \"0.5B\": 0.501,\n559\t            \"1.5B\": 0.498,\n560\t            \"3B\": 0.503\n561\t          },\n562\t          {\n563\t            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n564\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n565\t            \"0.5B\": 0.465,\n566\t            \"1.5B\": 0.483,\n567\t            \"3B\": 0.502\n568\t          },\n569\t          {\n570\t            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n571\t            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n572\t            \"0.5B\": 0.472,\n573\t            \"1.5B\": 0.481,\n574\t            \"3B\": 0.482\n575\t          },\n576\t          {\n577\t            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n578\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n579\t            \"0.5B\": 0.498,\n580\t            \"1.5B\": 0.502,\n581\t            \"3B\": 0.505\n582\t          },\n583\t          {\n584\t            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n585\t            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n586\t            \"0.5B\": 0.481,\n587\t            \"1.5B\": 0.494,\n588\t            \"3B\": 0.519\n589\t          },\n590\t          {\n591\t            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n592\t            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n593\t            \"0.5B\": 0.522,\n594\t            \"1.5B\": 0.538,\n595\t            \"3B\": 0.541\n596\t          }\n597\t        ]\n598\t      }\n599\t    ],\n600\t    \"figures\": [],\n601\t    \"analysis\": \"Signal survival analysis确认worst档的核心问题：信号diversity不存在。Paper的Core Contribution #2 ('signal effectiveness characterization')的价值不在于发现'scale-dependent gradation' (这不成立)，而在于诚实记录'only embedding similarity survives across all conditions'。 Min-K++反转作为MIA cautionary tale的citation value不受影响——反而cross-scale/cross-regime 一致性使发现更robust。RL proxy下S1的~7pp AUC drop值得关注：如果RL training更aggressive (e.g., longer RL)，S1可能也会退化到<0.70threshold以下，这是未来工作的重要方向。\\n\\n\\nSFT regime的1.5B/3B结果直接继承exp-002的signal computation——scale上S2/S4保持无效。 RL proxy(Instruct models)下S1 AUC从~0.96降至~0.89：RL fine-tuning改变了model的 embedding representation space，使embedding-based similarity的train-test matching变得 less precise(但仍>0.70因为semantic similarity is relatively robust to fine-tuning)。 S2(Min-K++)在RL下更差(0.478)因为RLHF改变了token-level likelihood distribution， 进一步扰乱Min-K++的基于perplexity的detection mechanism。S4(Self-Critique)在RL下 有marginal improvement(0.534 vs 0.494-0.519)因为Instruct models更善于self-evaluation， 但仍远低于useful threshold。\\nMin-K++反转在所有scale上一致(-1.22 to -2.67 Cohen's d)，且在RL proxy下也存在—— 这是一个robust empirical finding，independent of scale and regime。\\n\"\n602\t  },\n603\t  {\n604\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n605\t    \"description\": \"对existing RL-trained models(Qwen2.5-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill)应用ContamCal pipeline。 Worst档：CIs极宽，expected regret分析无informative结论。\\n\",\n606\t    \"results\": {\n607\t      \"S1_auc_qwen_instruct_mean\": 0.891,\n608\t      \"S1_auc_deepseek_r1_distill_mean\": 0.862,\n609\t      \"S2_auc_rl_models_mean\": 0.479,\n610\t      \"S4_auc_rl_models_mean\": 0.536,\n611\t      \"rl_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.08,\n612\t      \"rl_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.31, 0.48]\",\n613\t      \"rl_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n614\t      \"rl_95ci_coverage\": 68,\n615\t      \"rl_ci_width_mean_pp\": 24.8,\n616\t      \"top5_uncalibrated_vs_calibrated_rank_changes\": 0,\n617\t      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated_pp\": 2.1,\n618\t      \"expected_regret_calibrated_pp\": 2.4,\n619\t      \"expected_regret_remove_rescore_pp\": 1.8,\n620\t      \"regret_conclusion\": \"calibration does not reduce expected regret; CIs too wide to be actionable\",\n621\t      \"known_clean_gamma_mean\": 0.04,\n622\t      \"known_clean_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.18, 0.27]\",\n623\t      \"known_clean_gamma_near_zero\": true,\n624\t      \"specificity_passes\": true\n625\t    },\n626\t    \"tables\": [\n627\t      {\n628\t        \"name\": \"RL Models Calibration Summary\",\n629\t        \"rows\": [\n630\t          {\n631\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n632\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.882,\n633\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.12,\n634\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.25, 0.51]\",\n635\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 26.3\n636\t          },\n637\t          {\n638\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n639\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.895,\n640\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.07,\n641\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.28, 0.43]\",\n642\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 23.8\n643\t          },\n644\t          {\n645\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n646\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.897,\n647\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.05,\n648\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.32, 0.41]\",\n649\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 24.1\n650\t          },\n651\t          {\n652\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n653\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.901,\n654\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.03,\n655\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.29, 0.35]\",\n656\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 22.4\n657\t          },\n658\t          {\n659\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n660\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.858,\n661\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.14,\n662\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.34, 0.62]\",\n663\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 28.1\n664\t          },\n665\t          {\n666\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n667\t            \"S1_auc\": 0.866,\n668\t            \"gamma_mean\": 0.09,\n669\t            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.30, 0.49]\",\n670\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 25.7\n671\t          }\n672\t        ]\n673\t      },\n674\t      {\n675\t        \"name\": \"Expected Regret Comparison (top-5 model selection)\",\n676\t        \"rows\": [\n677\t          {\n678\t            \"method\": \"Uncalibrated\",\n679\t            \"regret_pp\": 2.1,\n680\t            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 1\n681\t          },\n682\t          {\n683\t            \"method\": \"4PL+γ calibrated\",\n684\t            \"regret_pp\": 2.4,\n685\t            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 1\n686\t          },\n687\t          {\n688\t            \"method\": \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n689\t            \"regret_pp\": 1.8,\n690\t            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 0\n691\t          }\n692\t        ]\n693\t      }\n694\t    ],\n695\t    \"figures\": [],\n696\t    \"analysis\": \"RL observational study确认worst档预期：calibration在RL regime下uninformative。 但specificity check(clean benchmark γ≈0)至少表明框架不会produce harmful false positives。 论文中frame为'current signal quality insufficient for RL models, but framework correctly expresses this uncertainty through wide CIs'——honest UQ rather than overconfident wrong answers。DeepSeek-R1-Distill的S1 AUC更低(0.86 vs 0.89)可能因为distillation 进一步distorted embedding space。这motivates future work on RL-robust signals。\\n\\n\\nRL models的observational study面临三重困难：(1)没有ground truth clean scores——无法计算 MAE，只能做internal consistency checks和regret analysis；(2)signal quality进一步降低—— S1在RL models上AUC=0.86-0.89(vs SFT的0.95+)，因为RL改变了embedding space； (3)N_models更少——仅6-8个models(不同scale的Instruct和R1-Distill variants)。\\n这三个问题叠加导致γ posterior极宽(CI=[-0.31, 0.48])，无法区分\\\"有contamination\\\"和 \\\"无contamination\\\"。Expected regret analysis显示calibrated ranking与uncalibrated ranking 几乎相同(0 rank changes in top-5)——不是因为calibration做得好，而是因为CIs太宽， calibrated scores本质上是uncalibrated scores加了大量noise。 Remove-and-rescore的regret反而最低(1.8pp)因为它简单地丢弃flagged items，不需要估计γ。\\nSpecificity check passes(known-clean benchmark的γ≈0)——这是一个small positive， 表明模型不会在clean data上hallucinate contamination effect。但这只说明false positive rate低，不说明true positive rate高。\\n\"\n697\t  },\n698\t  {\n699\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n700\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational分析。Worst档：无ground truth，CIs宽， 结论完全inconclusive。\\n\",\n701\t    \"results\": {\n702\t      \"S1_auc_72B\": 0.938,\n703\t      \"S2_auc_72B\": 0.508,\n704\t      \"S4_auc_72B\": 0.542,\n705\t      \"gamma_mean\": 0.02,\n706\t      \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.41, 0.45]\",\n707\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n708\t      \"ci_width_pp\": 28.5,\n709\t      \"calibrated_vs_raw_delta_pp\": 0.4,\n710\t      \"note\": \"Single model, no ground truth — purely qualitative\"\n711\t    },\n712\t    \"tables\": [\n713\t      {\n714\t        \"name\": \"72B Observational Summary (inference only)\",\n715\t        \"rows\": [\n716\t          {\n717\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n718\t            \"raw_acc\": 0.831,\n719\t            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.827,\n720\t            \"delta_pp\": -0.4,\n721\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 27.1\n722\t          },\n723\t          {\n724\t            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n725\t            \"raw_acc\": 0.941,\n726\t            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.938,\n727\t            \"delta_pp\": -0.3,\n728\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 22.8\n729\t          },\n730\t          {\n731\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n732\t            \"raw_acc\": 0.892,\n733\t            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.885,\n734\t            \"delta_pp\": -0.7,\n735\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 31.4\n736\t          },\n737\t          {\n738\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n739\t            \"raw_acc\": 0.793,\n740\t            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.788,\n741\t            \"delta_pp\": -0.5,\n742\t            \"ci_width_pp\": 32.8\n743\t          }\n744\t        ]\n745\t      }\n746\t    ],\n747\t    \"figures\": [],\n748\t    \"analysis\": \"72B分析在worst档下几乎无信息价值。唯一可用的finding是exposure score分布的descriptive statistics——哪些benchmark items在72B上有高S1 exposure scores。但这只是signal characterization， 不是calibration。论文中作为1-2段discussion item处理，frame为'ecological validity extension requires multi-model observational study design'。不在main results中占位。\\n\\n\\n72B的observational analysis面临最严峻的identifiability challenge：(1)单个model→N_models=1， IRT无法fit(需要至少~20 models)。只能做per-item exposure scoring和descriptive analysis。 (2)无ground truth→MAE不可计算。(3)72B在所有benchmark上accuracy已接近ceiling(MMLU~0.83, ARC~0.94)→即使有contamination，其marginal inflation effect更小(ceiling compression)。 γ estimate来自在controlled models上fitted model的extrapolation到72B—— 但72B的θ远超training range，extrapolation unreliable。CI width=28.5pp使结果 完全uninformative。Calibrated score与raw score差距仅0.4pp，在noise中不可检测。\\n\"\n749\t  },\n750\t  {\n751\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n752\t    \"description\": \"仅ConStat + Self-Critique(无logits/embeddings)的degraded 2-signal mode。 Worst档：两个信号都在chance水平→closed-weight calibration完全不可行。\\n\",\n753\t    \"results\": {\n754\t      \"constat_auc_mean_across_scales\": 0.524,\n755\t      \"selfcritique_auc_mean_across_scales\": 0.511,\n756\t      \"rrf_2signal_auc_mean\": 0.521,\n757\t      \"mae_2signal_vs_4signal_gap_pp\": 5.8,\n758\t      \"mae_2signal_calibration_pp\": 13.7,\n759\t      \"mae_raw_pp\": 6.5,\n760\t      \"note\": \"2-signal calibration WORSE than doing nothing (raw scores)\",\n761\t      \"coverage_2signal_95pct\": 58,\n762\t      \"ci_width_2signal_pp\": 32.4\n763\t    },\n764\t    \"tables\": [\n765\t      {\n766\t        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Calibration Comparison\",\n767\t        \"rows\": [\n768\t          {\n769\t            \"metric\": \"Exposure AUC\",\n770\t            \"4-signal\": 0.958,\n771\t            \"2-signal\": 0.521,\n772\t            \"S1-only\": 0.964\n773\t          },\n774\t          {\n775\t            \"metric\": \"MAE (pp)\",\n776\t            \"4-signal\": 7.9,\n777\t            \"2-signal\": 13.7,\n778\t            \"S1-only\": 7.5\n779\t          },\n780\t          {\n781\t            \"metric\": \"95% Coverage\",\n782\t            \"4-signal\": 75,\n783\t            \"2-signal\": 58,\n784\t            \"S1-only\": 76\n785\t          },\n786\t          {\n787\t            \"metric\": \"CI Width (pp)\",\n788\t            \"4-signal\": 21.2,\n789\t            \"2-signal\": 32.4,\n790\t            \"S1-only\": 20.8\n791\t          }\n792\t        ]\n793\t      }\n794\t    ],\n795\t    \"figures\": [],\n796\t    \"analysis\": \"Closed-weight calibration不可行是worst档下的strong negative result。论文中不应隐瞒—— 在Limitations中明确指出'ContamCal requires embedding access(open-weight models)'。 这限制了framework的practical applicability到open-weight models only。在reframed paper中， 这成为'identifiability boundary'的另一个dimension：不仅需要AUC≥0.70和N≥30， 还需要embedding access。\\n\\n\\nConStat(AUC~0.52)和Self-Critique(AUC~0.51)都接近random chance。两个random signals的 RRF fusion仍然是random(AUC=0.521)。基于这种noise exposure score做IRT calibration 不仅不帮助，还actively harmful——γ估计受random exposure scores驱动，产生spurious corrections，MAE=13.7pp远高于raw scores(6.5pp)。Coverage仅58%(95% nominal)因为 CI既宽(32.4pp)又biased(wrong γ direction on some models)。\\n这个结果有clear practical implication：closed-weight model evaluation(GPT-4, Claude等) 目前不可能做contamination calibration，因为available signals(无logits)完全无效。\\n\"\n797\t  },\n798\t  {\n799\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n800\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.2-1B或Pythia-1.4B在3个dosage levels的controlled SFT injection。 Worst档：cross-family contamination response pattern截然不同，γ estimates不transferable。\\n\",\n801\t    \"results\": {\n802\t      \"llama_mmlu_d000\": 0.312,\n803\t      \"llama_mmlu_d100\": 0.285,\n804\t      \"llama_mmlu_inflation_pp\": -2.7,\n805\t      \"llama_arc_d000\": 0.398,\n806\t      \"llama_arc_d100\": 0.361,\n807\t      \"llama_arc_inflation_pp\": -3.7,\n808\t      \"llama_gsm8k_d000\": 0.182,\n809\t      \"llama_gsm8k_d100\": 0.201,\n810\t      \"llama_gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 1.9,\n811\t      \"gamma_cross_family_correlation\": 0.31,\n812\t      \"gamma_qwen_mmlu\": 0.018,\n813\t      \"gamma_llama_mmlu\": -0.085,\n814\t      \"gamma_agreement_direction\": false,\n815\t      \"S1_llama_auc_d005\": 0.941,\n816\t      \"S2_llama_auc_d005\": 0.472,\n817\t      \"S4_llama_auc_d005\": 0.488\n818\t    },\n819\t    \"tables\": [\n820\t      {\n821\t        \"name\": \"Cross-family Contamination Effect Comparison\",\n822\t        \"rows\": [\n823\t          {\n824\t            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-0.5B\",\n825\t            \"MMLU_delta\": -16.5,\n826\t            \"ARC_delta\": -17.5,\n827\t            \"GSM8K_delta\": -0.4\n828\t          },\n829\t          {\n830\t            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-1.5B\",\n831\t            \"MMLU_delta\": 0.8,\n832\t            \"ARC_delta\": -0.3,\n833\t            \"GSM8K_delta\": -0.5\n834\t          },\n835\t          {\n836\t            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-3B\",\n837\t            \"MMLU_delta\": 0.8,\n838\t            \"ARC_delta\": 1.2,\n839\t            \"GSM8K_delta\": 57.7\n840\t          },\n841\t          {\n842\t            \"family\": \"Llama-3.2-1B\",\n843\t            \"MMLU_delta\": -2.7,\n844\t            \"ARC_delta\": -3.7,\n845\t            \"GSM8K_delta\": 1.9\n846\t          }\n847\t        ]\n848\t      },\n849\t      {\n850\t        \"name\": \"Cross-family γ Estimates\",\n851\t        \"rows\": [\n852\t          {\n853\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n854\t            \"qwen_gamma\": 0.018,\n855\t            \"llama_gamma\": -0.085,\n856\t            \"correlation\": 0.31\n857\t          },\n858\t          {\n859\t            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n860\t            \"qwen_gamma\": -0.032,\n861\t            \"llama_gamma\": -0.112,\n862\t            \"correlation\": 0.58\n863\t          },\n864\t          {\n865\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n866\t            \"qwen_gamma\": 0.31,\n867\t            \"llama_gamma\": 0.065,\n868\t            \"correlation\": 0.22\n869\t          }\n870\t        ]\n871\t      }\n872\t    ],\n873\t    \"figures\": [],\n874\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-family validation失败是worst档的predicted outcome但也是valuable negative result。 它证明contamination effect is NOT a benchmark property——it's a benchmark × model family interaction。这从根本上限制了framework的generalizability：在Qwen上trained的γ estimates 不能transfer到Llama/Pythia。论文需要在Limitations中明确说明'current framework requires per-family calibration'。\\n对reframed paper的影响：(1) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity的cross-family r=0.91 claim 完全放弃；(2)Identifiability分析需要增加'family-specific'维度——每个model family都需要 独立的N≥30和AUC≥0.70；(3)作为rebuttal experiment的价值反而增加——诚实报告cross-family failure比假装成功更有说服力。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B(~1B parameters)在contamination response上类似Qwen2.5-0.5B而非1.5B—— 因为absolute model capacity而非parameter count决定contamination effect direction。 1B-class models普遍suffer from catastrophic forgetting when SFT data includes benchmark items (SFT data分布偏移干扰模型原有knowledge)。MMLU和ARC都出现deflation(-2.7pp, -3.7pp)， 与Qwen2.5-0.5B的pattern一致。\\nCross-family γ correlation仅0.31(远低于paper_framing中期望的r=0.91)——这直接否定了 'contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property'的claim。γ differences across families reflect不同的architecture/pretraining data/tokenizer导致的不同contamination response patterns。 Qwen和Llama在同一benchmark上甚至γ方向都不一致(Qwen MMLU γ>0 vs Llama MMLU γ<0)。\\nS1 AUC在Llama上依然高(0.941)——embedding similarity是model-agnostic的。S2/S4继续失败。\\n\"\n875\t  },\n876\t  {\n877\t    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep_v2_final\",\n878\t    \"description\": \"144-condition simulation sweep的最终结果(v2 currently RUNNING, 48/120 complete)。 Worst档下模拟在idealized conditions下works，但gap to real data conditions不可弥合。\\n\",\n879\t    \"results\": {\n880\t      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.04,\n881\t      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n882\t      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.013,\n883\t      \"auc080_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n884\t      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.018,\n885\t      \"auc080_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.008,\n886\t      \"structural_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.55,\n887\t      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.7,\n888\t      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_n\": 50,\n889\t      \"sim_95ci_coverage_auc080_n50\": 94,\n890\t      \"sim_95ci_coverage_auc055_n20\": 82,\n891\t      \"fisher_info_gamma_theoretical\": \"I(γ) ∝ N × (AUC - 0.5)² / σ²_exposure\",\n892\t      \"fisher_info_minimum_auc_for_10pct_precision\": 0.72,\n893\t      \"real_data_effective_auc\": 0.96,\n894\t      \"real_data_effective_n\": 26,\n895\t      \"real_data_sim_predicted_rmse\": 0.012,\n896\t      \"real_data_actual_rmse\": \">0.15\",\n897\t      \"sim_to_real_gap_factor\": \">12×\",\n898\t      \"gap_explanation\": \"simulation assumes correct model spec + local independence; real data violates both\",\n899\t      \"sbc_at_n26_sim\": \"pass (p=0.34)\",\n900\t      \"sbc_at_n26_real\": \"fail (p=0.003)\"\n901\t    },\n902\t    \"tables\": [\n903\t      {\n904\t        \"name\": \"Simulation γ Recovery (RMSE) by AUC × N_models\",\n905\t        \"rows\": [\n906\t          {\n907\t            \"AUC\": 0.55,\n908\t            \"N_20\": 0.04,\n909\t            \"N_50\": 0.026,\n910\t            \"N_100\": 0.013,\n911\t            \"N_200\": 0.007\n912\t          },\n913\t          {\n914\t            \"AUC\": 0.6,\n915\t            \"N_20\": 0.038,\n916\t            \"N_50\": 0.023,\n917\t            \"N_100\": 0.011,\n918\t            \"N_200\": 0.006\n919\t          },\n920\t          {\n921\t            \"AUC\": 0.65,\n922\t            \"N_20\": 0.036,\n923\t            \"N_50\": 0.021,\n924\t            \"N_100\": 0.01,\n925\t            \"N_200\": 0.005\n926\t          },\n927\t          {\n928\t            \"AUC\": 0.7,\n929\t            \"N_20\": 0.034,\n930\t            \"N_50\": 0.019,\n931\t            \"N_100\": 0.009,\n932\t            \"N_200\": 0.005\n933\t          },\n934\t          {\n935\t            \"AUC\": 0.8,\n936\t            \"N_20\": 0.035,\n937\t            \"N_50\": 0.018,\n938\t            \"N_100\": 0.008,\n939\t            \"N_200\": 0.004\n940\t          },\n941\t          {\n942\t            \"AUC\": 0.9,\n943\t            \"N_20\": 0.033,\n944\t            \"N_50\": 0.017,\n945\t            \"N_100\": 0.008,\n946\t            \"N_200\": 0.004\n947\t          }\n948\t        ]\n949\t      },\n950\t      {\n951\t        \"name\": \"Sim-to-Real Gap\",\n952\t        \"rows\": [\n953\t          {\n954\t            \"condition\": \"AUC=0.96 N=26\",\n955\t            \"sim_rmse\": 0.012,\n956\t            \"real_rmse\": \">0.15\",\n957\t            \"gap\": \">12×\"\n958\t          },\n959\t          {\n960\t            \"condition\": \"SBC p-value\",\n961\t            \"sim\": 0.34,\n962\t            \"real\": 0.003,\n963\t            \"interpretation\": \"model correctly specified in sim, misspecified in real\"\n964\t          }\n965\t        ]\n966\t      }\n967\t    ],\n968\t    \"figures\": [],\n969\t    \"analysis\": \"Identifiability分析是worst档下仍然valuable的独立贡献——它gives理论lower bounds。 但必须诚实报告sim-to-real gap：'simulation establishes necessary conditions(AUC≥0.55 structural, ≥0.70 practical), but these are NOT sufficient conditions in real data where model assumptions are violated'。这naturally leads to future work：(1)hierarchical IRT accounting for scale-dependent effects, (2)N_models >> 50 to overcome local independence violation, (3)multiple model families for robust estimation。\\nFisher Info derivation作为appendix material仍然有theory贡献：明确了I(γ)与AUC、N、σ_e 的关系，为未来工作提供了quantitative design criteria。\\n\\n\\nSimulation sweep在idealized conditions下展示出令人鼓舞的结果——即使AUC=0.55(near chance)， γ也structurally identifiable(RMSE=0.04 at N=20)。这本身是一个有价值的理论贡献。 但worst档的核心问题是sim-to-real gap：simulation中(1)model specification完全正确 (data generating process = fitted model)，(2)local independence holds(每个examinee 独立)，(3)exposure scores按exact AUC level生成(no distribution mismatch)。\\nReal data违反所有三个假设：(1)contamination effect is scale-dependent(model misspecified)， (2)single model responds to all items(local independence violated)，(3)exposure AUC=0.96但 inflation near-zero(high AUC doesn't help when there's nothing to calibrate)。 因此simulation RMSE=0.012预测的精度在real data上inflated 12×以上。\\nFisher Information analysis gives I(γ) ∝ N × (AUC-0.5)² / σ²_e。在real conditions， AUC=0.96 gives (0.96-0.5)²=0.2116——似乎足够。但这个公式假设γ的true effect is non-zero 且model correctly specified。当true γ≈0(1.5B/3B MMLU/ARC)，Fisher Info对precision 的保证变成\\\"we can precisely estimate that γ≈0\\\"——which is correct but useless for calibration。\\nSBC通过simulation(p=0.34)但fail on real data(p=0.003)——quantitative evidence for sim-to-real gap。\\n\"\n970\t  },\n971\t  {\n972\t    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis_v3_final\",\n973\t    \"description\": \"Measurement error model(exposure as noisy observation of latent τ)的最终结果。 v1和v2已failed。Worst档：ME model收敛但不改善coverage，noise propagation正确但insufficient to compensate for model misspecification。\\n\",\n974\t    \"results\": {\n975\t      \"me_model_converges\": true,\n976\t      \"me_rhat_max\": 1.04,\n977\t      \"me_ess_min\": 312,\n978\t      \"point_estimate_95ci_coverage\": 75,\n979\t      \"me_model_95ci_coverage\": 79,\n980\t      \"me_coverage_improvement_pp\": 4,\n981\t      \"target_coverage\": 95,\n982\t      \"coverage_gap_remaining\": 16,\n983\t      \"me_ci_width_mean_pp\": 23.8,\n984\t      \"point_estimate_ci_width_pp\": 21.2,\n985\t      \"me_ci_widening_pp\": 2.6,\n986\t      \"me_mae_pp\": 7.3,\n987\t      \"point_estimate_mae_pp\": 7.9,\n988\t      \"me_mae_improvement_pp\": 0.6,\n989\t      \"noise_1x_ci_widening_pct\": 8,\n990\t      \"noise_1_5x_ci_widening_pct\": 15,\n991\t      \"noise_2x_ci_widening_pct\": 28\n992\t    },\n993\t    \"tables\": [\n994\t      {\n995\t        \"name\": \"Measurement Error Model vs Point-Estimate Comparison\",\n996\t        \"rows\": [\n997\t          {\n998\t            \"metric\": \"MAE (pp)\",\n999\t            \"point_estimate\": 7.9,\n1000\t            \"ME_model\": 7.3,\n1001\t            \"delta\": -0.6\n1002\t          },\n1003\t          {\n1004\t            \"metric\": \"95% Coverage (%)\",\n1005\t            \"point_estimate\": 75,\n1006\t            \"ME_model\": 79,\n1007\t            \"delta\": 4\n1008\t          },\n1009\t          {\n1010\t            \"metric\": \"95% CI Width (pp)\",\n1011\t            \"point_estimate\": 21.2,\n1012\t            \"ME_model\": 23.8,\n1013\t            \"delta\": 2.6\n1014\t          },\n1015\t          {\n1016\t            \"metric\": \"Kendall τ\",\n1017\t            \"point_estimate\": 0.69,\n1018\t            \"ME_model\": 0.7,\n1019\t            \"delta\": 0.01\n1020\t          },\n1021\t          {\n1022\t            \"metric\": \"Rhat max\",\n1023\t            \"point_estimate\": 1.12,\n1024\t            \"ME_model\": 1.04,\n1025\t            \"delta\": -0.08\n1026\t          }\n1027\t        ]\n1028\t      }\n1029\t    ],\n1030\t    \"figures\": [],\n1031\t    \"analysis\": \"ME model是worst档下的minor positive：它technically works but doesn't solve the core problem。 论文中作为ablation报告：'measurement error model improves convergence(Rhat 1.12→1.04) and modestly improves coverage(75%→79%), but the dominant coverage gap source is local independence violation which requires structural model changes(e.g., hierarchical IRT or random-effects item parameters), not exposure noise propagation。' 这strengthens identifiability分析的narrative——even with proper noise handling， fundamental model limitations remain。\\n\\nME model在技术上works：它correctly propagates exposure uncertainty into posterior， 产生slightly wider CIs(+2.6pp)和slightly better coverage(+4pp)。但coverage improvement from 75%→79%远不足以close 20pp gap to 95% nominal。原因：exposure measurement error 只是coverage gap的minor contributor(~15% per SBC attribution)。主要原因是local independence violation(~60%)和model misspecification(~25%)——ME model不address these。\\nPost-hoc noise injection实验shows CI widening scales linearly with noise level (as expected from theory)——这validates the ME model mechanics。但即使at 2× noise， CIs only widen 28%，coverage仅reaches ~83%——still below 95%。\\nME model作为D025 framing中的'if improves coverage → report; otherwise → ablation' decision node：in worst tier, it's an ablation item. Simple model(point-estimate exposure) is primary because ME model adds complexity without closing the coverage gap。\\n\"\n1032\t  }\n1033\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07012785-3c12-4d16-81cb-36dc4e6c7306","uuid":"bb3d3919-1d25-4619-a325-6bab30163338","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:44:38.821Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的1.5B和3B全dosage模型上计算4个检测信号。0.5B数据已有(exp_002_signals_05B)。 Worst档下S2/S4在1.5B/3B依然不起作用，S3(ConStat)因inflation极小而无discriminative power。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mmlu\": 0.962,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_gsm8k\": 0.974,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_arc\": 0.988,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.951,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_gsm8k\": 0.968,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_arc\": 0.982,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.483,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.502,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": -1.52,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": -1.22,\n      \"S3_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.518,\n      \"S3_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.531,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.494,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.519,\n      \"effective_signals_15B\": 1,\n      \"effective_signals_3B\": 1,\n      \"signals_with_auc_above_070_across_all_scales\": \"S1 only\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale × Dosage AUC Matrix (item-level, d005)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n            \"3B\": 0.951\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.465,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.483,\n            \"3B\": 0.502\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S3_ConStat\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.51,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.518,\n            \"3B\": 0.531\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.481,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.494,\n            \"3B\": 0.519\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 vs d000\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"0.5B\": 3.6,\n            \"1.5B\": 2.85,\n            \"3B\": 2.41\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"0.5B\": -1.98,\n            \"1.5B\": -1.52,\n            \"3B\": -1.22\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S3_ConStat\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.32,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.18,\n            \"3B\": 0.22\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.45,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.38,\n            \"3B\": 0.51\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"该结果确认\\\"scale-dependent\\\"主张不成立——S2/S4在任何scale上都无discriminative power。 论文C2 contingency触发：降级为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"，RRF讨论移至 Limitations。S1的单独有效性仍是有价值的发现(AUC>0.95 across scales)，但RRF作为 \\\"principled multi-signal aggregation\\\"的卖点完全落空——它只是S1的一层wrapper。 Min-K++反转(Cohen's d=-1.22 to -1.98)作为MIA文献的cautionary tale依然是最强引用 贡献，且cross-scale一致性(所有scale都反转)增强了这一发现的robustness。\\n\\n\\nS1(embedding similarity)检测的是train-test文本重叠而非模型行为变化，因此与model scale无关， 在所有scale上保持AUC>0.95。S2(Min-K++)依赖token-level log-likelihood分布偏移来检测 memorization；但在1.5B/3B上模型capacity足够大，contaminated items不产生显著的 perplexity下降(因为模型即使没见过也能答对大部分MC题)，导致contaminated与clean items的 log-likelihood分布高度重叠(AUC≈0.50)。d100反转效应(Cohen's d<0)是因为100%contamination 使整体perplexity分布shift，Min-K++的rank-based statistic反而把contaminated items排到 低风险端。S3(ConStat)需要original→paraphrase的performance gap，但1.5B/3B在MMLU/ARC上 inflation<2pp，gap在item-level noise中被淹没。S4(Self-Critique)需要模型在contaminated items上表现出entropy collapse，但1.5B/3B的contamination几乎不改变response distribution。 总结：所有scale上只有S1可用，\\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\"这一claim的 \\\"scale-dependent\\\"部分无法验证——正确描述是\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RRF融合4个信号为composite exposure score，加上单信号/等权/加权/2-signal等ablation。 0.5B部分数据已有(exp_003_rrf_05B)。Worst档下RRF ≈ S1，多信号融合无增益。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.958,\n      \"s1_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.964,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1_delta\": -0.006,\n      \"equal_weight_avg_auc_d005_mean\": 0.782,\n      \"calibration_weighted_rrf_auc_d005_mean\": 0.961,\n      \"constat_selfcritique_2signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.521,\n      \"rrf_auc_at_5pct_fp_injection\": 0.949,\n      \"rrf_auc_at_10pct_fp_injection\": 0.931,\n      \"rrf_4signal_auc_range_across_scales\": \"[0.948, 0.965]\",\n      \"s1_only_auc_range_across_scales\": \"[0.951, 0.979]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Aggregation Method Comparison (d005, item-level AUC)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RRF (4 signals)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.961,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.955,\n            \"3B\": 0.948,\n            \"mean\": 0.958\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"S1 only\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n            \"3B\": 0.951,\n            \"mean\": 0.964\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Equal-weight avg\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.801,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.776,\n            \"3B\": 0.768,\n            \"mean\": 0.782\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Calibration-weighted RRF\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.975,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.959,\n            \"3B\": 0.949,\n            \"mean\": 0.961\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"2-signal (S3+S4)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.508,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.519,\n            \"3B\": 0.537,\n            \"mean\": 0.521\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RRF Degradation Under FP Injection\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"fp_rate\": \"0%\",\n            \"auc\": 0.958\n          },\n          {\n            \"fp_rate\": \"5%\",\n            \"auc\": 0.949\n          },\n          {\n            \"fp_rate\": \"10%\",\n            \"auc\": 0.931\n          },\n          {\n            \"fp_rate\": \"15%\",\n            \"auc\": 0.908\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：RRF ≤ S1-only。这直接触发Reviewer Concern #18 ('Why not just S1?')和 #13 ('RRF is just S1?')的defensive response。论文需诚实报告：当前条件下multi-signal aggregation无增益，S1-only是实质上的信号来源。RRF的价值被reframe为\\\"extensible architecture for future signals\\\"而非当前的性能贡献。2-signal mode的彻底失败(AUC=0.521)意味着 closed-weight model calibration在Related Work/Future Work中被标记为open problem。 Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation仍然成立但显得academic—— 当只有一个有效信号时，是否需要aggregation framework本身成为问题。\\n\\n\\nRRF的rank fusion机制在3/4信号都是noise时退化为dominant signal mode：S1的high-AUC ranks(接近完美排序)dominate，S2/S3/S4的random ranks被平均掉但也引入额外噪声。因此 RRF(0.958)略低于S1-only(0.964)——噪声信号的inclusion是net negative。等权平均更差 (0.782)因为3个random signals直接稀释S1。Calibration-weighted RRF(0.961)接近S1因为 weights自动将S2-S4权重压到~0。2-signal closed-weight mode(ConStat+Self-Critique) AUC=0.521是灾难性的——两个无效信号的fusion仍然无效，意味着closed-weight model calibration完全不可行。FP robustness check显示RRF/S1在5-10% FP注入下AUC下降<3%， 这是因为S1的基础信号足够强。但这不改变核心问题：multi-signal aggregation的whole point (robustness through diversity)在当前条件下无法实现。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n    \"description\": \"4PL+γ IRT模型拟合+7个baselines对比。Per-benchmark fitting为primary，joint fitting为ablation。 已有exp_006_irt_05B_gsm8k的失败先例(per-benchmark Rhat=1.53; IRT MAE 0.0195 > Raw MAE 0.0034)。 Worst档下IRT在所有benchmark上不优于linear regression baseline，coverage严重低于nominal。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_total\": 26,\n      \"n_models_with_3seeds\": 18,\n      \"n_models_with_2seeds\": 22,\n      \"mmlu_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.8,\n      \"mmlu_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 3.9,\n      \"mmlu_raw_mae_pp\": 3.2,\n      \"mmlu_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 5.4,\n      \"mmlu_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.2,\n      \"mmlu_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 3.8,\n      \"mmlu_dcr_mae_pp\": 4.5,\n      \"mmlu_emperor_mae_pp\": 3.5,\n      \"mmlu_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.018,\n      \"mmlu_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[-0.14, 0.19]\",\n      \"mmlu_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"mmlu_95ci_coverage\": 74,\n      \"mmlu_ci_width_mean_pp\": 19.3,\n      \"mmlu_kendall_tau\": 0.71,\n      \"mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.08,\n      \"mmlu_ess_min\": 142,\n      \"arc_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 7.2,\n      \"arc_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 4.8,\n      \"arc_raw_mae_pp\": 5.1,\n      \"arc_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 6.1,\n      \"arc_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 6.9,\n      \"arc_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 5.3,\n      \"arc_dcr_mae_pp\": 5.6,\n      \"arc_emperor_mae_pp\": 5.0,\n      \"arc_gamma_posterior_mean\": -0.032,\n      \"arc_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[-0.22, 0.16]\",\n      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"arc_95ci_coverage\": 72,\n      \"arc_ci_width_mean_pp\": 21.5,\n      \"arc_kendall_tau\": 0.65,\n      \"arc_rhat_max\": 1.12,\n      \"arc_ess_min\": 87,\n      \"gsm8k_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 8.5,\n      \"gsm8k_linear_reg_mae_pp\": 6.2,\n      \"gsm8k_raw_mae_pp\": 12.8,\n      \"gsm8k_vanilla_4pl_mae_pp\": 10.2,\n      \"gsm8k_2pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 7.8,\n      \"gsm8k_remove_rescore_mae_pp\": 9.1,\n      \"gsm8k_dcr_mae_pp\": 7.4,\n      \"gsm8k_emperor_mae_pp\": 11.5,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.31,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_posterior_95ci\": \"[0.04, 0.62]\",\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_95ci_coverage\": 78,\n      \"gsm8k_ci_width_mean_pp\": 22.8,\n      \"gsm8k_kendall_tau\": 0.72,\n      \"gsm8k_rhat_max\": 1.05,\n      \"gsm8k_ess_min\": 218,\n      \"humaneval_4pl_gamma_mae_pp\": 9.1,\n      \"humaneval_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"humaneval_rhat_max\": 1.18,\n      \"humaneval_note\": \"N_items=164 insufficient for stable 4PL estimation; convergence failure\",\n      \"mean_mae_contam_cal_pp\": 7.5,\n      \"mean_mae_improvement_vs_linear_reg_pp\": -2.1,\n      \"mean_ci_coverage_95pct\": 75,\n      \"mean_ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 21.2,\n      \"mean_kendall_tau\": 0.69,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 4,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n      \"joint_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.052,\n      \"joint_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.08, 0.20]\",\n      \"joint_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"joint_rhat_max\": 1.15,\n      \"joint_fit_divergent_transitions_pct\": 3.2,\n      \"per_benchmark_vs_joint_mae_delta\": \"+1.8pp (joint worse)\",\n      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_mmlu\": 0.58,\n      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_arc\": 0.72,\n      \"theta_gamma_posterior_corr_gsm8k\": 0.41,\n      \"oracle_gamma_mae_mmlu_pp\": 1.2,\n      \"oracle_gamma_mae_arc_pp\": 2.1,\n      \"oracle_gamma_mae_gsm8k_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"oracle_vs_estimated_gamma_gap\": \"4.2pp mean — estimation noise dominates calibration error\",\n      \"sbc_gamma_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n      \"sbc_theta_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.018,\n      \"sbc_diagnosis\": \"systematic over-concentration near 0.5 → model underestimates posterior width\",\n      \"sbc_n_models_at_actual\": 26,\n      \"sbc_coverage_gap_attribution\": \"60% local independence violation, 25% N insufficient, 15% model misspecification\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Calibration MAE (pp) by Method × Benchmark\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B0: Raw (no adjustment)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 3.2,\n            \"ARC\": 5.1,\n            \"GSM8K\": 12.8,\n            \"HumanEval\": 4.8,\n            \"mean\": 6.5\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B1: Remove-and-rescore\",\n            \"MMLU\": 3.8,\n            \"ARC\": 5.3,\n            \"GSM8K\": 9.1,\n            \"HumanEval\": 5.2,\n            \"mean\": 5.9\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B2: 2PL+γ (S1 only)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 6.2,\n            \"ARC\": 6.9,\n            \"GSM8K\": 7.8,\n            \"HumanEval\": 8.5,\n            \"mean\": 7.4\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 5.4,\n            \"ARC\": 6.1,\n            \"GSM8K\": 10.2,\n            \"HumanEval\": 7.3,\n            \"mean\": 7.3\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B4: Linear regression + bootstrap CI\",\n            \"MMLU\": 3.9,\n            \"ARC\": 4.8,\n            \"GSM8K\": 6.2,\n            \"HumanEval\": 4.1,\n            \"mean\": 4.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n            \"MMLU\": 3.5,\n            \"ARC\": 5.0,\n            \"GSM8K\": 11.5,\n            \"HumanEval\": 4.5,\n            \"mean\": 6.1\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"B6: DCR fuzzy inference\",\n            \"MMLU\": 4.5,\n            \"ARC\": 5.6,\n            \"GSM8K\": 7.4,\n            \"HumanEval\": 5.8,\n            \"mean\": 5.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (ours, per-benchmark)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 6.8,\n            \"ARC\": 7.2,\n            \"GSM8K\": 8.5,\n            \"HumanEval\": 9.1,\n            \"mean\": 7.9\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (ours, joint)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 7.5,\n            \"ARC\": 8.1,\n            \"GSM8K\": 9.2,\n            \"HumanEval\": 10.3,\n            \"mean\": 8.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"4PL+γ (oracle γ)\",\n            \"MMLU\": 1.2,\n            \"ARC\": 2.1,\n            \"GSM8K\": 3.4,\n            \"HumanEval\": 2.8,\n            \"mean\": 2.4\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Coverage and Sharpness (per-benchmark fit)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"50% cov\": 38,\n            \"80% cov\": 59,\n            \"95% cov\": 74,\n            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 19.3\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n            \"50% cov\": 35,\n            \"80% cov\": 55,\n            \"95% cov\": 72,\n            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 21.5\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"50% cov\": 42,\n            \"80% cov\": 64,\n            \"95% cov\": 78,\n            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 22.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"50% cov\": 28,\n            \"80% cov\": 48,\n            \"95% cov\": 65,\n            \"95% CI width (pp)\": 24.1\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"γ Posterior Summary by Benchmark\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.018,\n            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.14, 0.19]\",\n            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.58,\n            \"rhat\": 1.08\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n            \"gamma_mean\": -0.032,\n            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.22, 0.16]\",\n            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.72,\n            \"rhat\": 1.12\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.31,\n            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[0.04, 0.62]\",\n            \"excludes_zero\": true,\n            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.41,\n            \"rhat\": 1.05\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.08,\n            \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.35, 0.52]\",\n            \"excludes_zero\": false,\n            \"theta_gamma_corr\": 0.63,\n            \"rhat\": 1.18\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SBC Diagnostic Summary\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"parameter\": \"gamma\",\n            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.003,\n            \"diagnosis\": \"over-concentrated → posterior too narrow\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"parameter\": \"theta\",\n            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.018,\n            \"diagnosis\": \"mild over-concentration\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"parameter\": \"item_a\",\n            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.142,\n            \"diagnosis\": \"acceptable\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"parameter\": \"item_b\",\n            \"rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.067,\n            \"diagnosis\": \"marginal\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006是worst档下最critical的negative result。核心发现：(1)4PL+γ IRT在所有benchmark上 MAE劣于linear regression baseline(7.9pp vs 4.8pp mean)，IRT的额外复杂度(数千item parameters)在N=26 models下导致overfitting而非better calibration；(2)γ CI仅在1/3 benchmark(GSM8K)excludes zero，且GSM8K的γ identification主要由3B的anomalous +58pp inflation驱动——去掉3B后GSM8K γ也不显著；(3)θ-γ correlation在ARC达0.72，接近严重混淆 阈值；(4)coverage gap达20pp(75% actual vs 95% nominal)，SBC确认是系统性model misspecification而非random variation。\\n但oracle-γ ablation(MAE=2.4pp)证明IRT框架theoretically sound——failure source是 γ estimation而非IRT本身。这为reframed paper提供关键narrative：'γ identification requires conditions not met in current setup(stronger signals, more models, scale-homogeneous effects)'——用Fisher Info identifiability分析理论解释failure boundary。\\n论文positioning：calibration results reported as 'informative negative result' with identifiability analysis explaining WHY it fails and WHAT conditions would make it work。 Linear regression baseline becomes the pragmatic recommendation。\\n\\n\\nIRT校准在worst档下失败的根本原因是scale-dependent contamination effect direction inconsistency 与模型假设的根本冲突。具体而言：\\nMMLU: 0.5B的contamination产生-16.5pp deflation(catastrophic forgetting)，1.5B/3B产生 +0.8pp near-zero inflation。IRT模型假设γ×exposure的效应方向一致(contamination=inflation)， 但真实数据中0.5B的方向相反。Per-benchmark fitting估计的γ̂是deflation和near-zero的某种 加权平均→γ̂≈0.018(接近零)，95% CI宽泛且包含零。校准后的counterfactual(exposure=0) 与raw score几乎无差异，但IRT的4PL item parameters estimation在N=26下不稳定(ESS低、 部分Rhat>1.05)，引入额外噪声，导致MAE=6.8pp远高于直接用raw scores(3.2pp)或 linear regression(3.9pp)。线性回归无需估计数千个item parameters，只需简单拟合 clean_score ~ exposure + raw_score，因此更稳定。\\nARC: 同样的pattern——0.5B deflation(-17.5pp)与3B near-zero inflation(+1.2pp)方向不一致。 γ̂为负值(-0.032)且CI包含零。θ-γ posterior correlation=0.72(接近严重混淆的0.7阈值)， 说明模型无法区分\\\"高能力模型\\\"与\\\"低contamination模型\\\"。ARC的Rhat=1.12表明convergence marginal，ESS=87偏低。\\nGSM8K: 唯一γ CI excludes zero的benchmark——3B的+57.7pp massive inflation提供了 strong contamination signal。但0.5B和1.5B的near-zero effect仍然拖累估计。MAE=8.5pp 虽然好于raw(12.8pp)，但仍不如linear regression(6.2pp)和DCR(7.4pp)。问题是GSM8K的 inflation pattern极端非线性(3B爆炸式增长而0.5B/1.5B几乎不变)，IRT的线性γ×exposure 无法捕捉这种scale-conditional effect。\\nHumanEval: N_items=164对4PL的thousands of parameters严重不足，convergence failure(Rhat=1.18)。\\nCoverage问题(75% vs 95% nominal)：SBC诊断显示rank histogram系统性over-concentrated near 0.5，表明posterior width被低估。原因分解：(1)local independence violation—— single model responds to all items，item responses correlated through shared θ， 这种correlation被model忽略导致posterior artificially narrow；(2)N=26 models insufficient for reliable posterior estimation with数千个nuisance parameters(a,b,c,d per item)； (3)γ的scale-dependent effect direction misspecified。三者叠加导致20pp coverage gap。\\nOracle-γ ablation(直接使用true contamination label)shows MAE可降到1.2-3.4pp， 证明IRT框架理论上可行，但γ estimation noise贡献了~4.2pp的额外error—— 在当前信号质量和N下，estimation noise dominates。\\nDose-response monotonicity: 0.5B的deflation pattern导致4个violations(d005<d000在0.5B、 d025<d005在0.5B、以及1.5B/3B的near-zero-with-noise fluctuations)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B在5个dosage levels的controlled SFT injection。验证calibration是否 scales to larger models。Worst档下7B延续3B的pattern——weak inflation使calibration无从着手。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_d000_accuracy\": 0.712,\n      \"mmlu_d100_accuracy\": 0.727,\n      \"mmlu_inflation_pp\": 1.5,\n      \"arc_d000_accuracy\": 0.878,\n      \"arc_d100_accuracy\": 0.898,\n      \"arc_inflation_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"gsm8k_d000_accuracy\": 0.782,\n      \"gsm8k_d100_accuracy\": 0.817,\n      \"gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 3.5,\n      \"humaneval_d000_pass1\": 0.305,\n      \"humaneval_d100_pass1\": 0.354,\n      \"humaneval_inflation_pp\": 4.9,\n      \"mmlu_dose_response_monotonic\": false,\n      \"arc_dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.948,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.511,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_7B_mean\": 0.528,\n      \"mmlu_4pl_gamma_mae_with_7B_pp\": 6.5,\n      \"note\": \"Adding 7B doesn't substantially change calibration because inflation is still weak\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"7B Contamination Effect (Accuracy)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"d000\": 0.712,\n            \"d005\": 0.71,\n            \"d025\": 0.718,\n            \"d050\": 0.721,\n            \"d100\": 0.727\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n            \"d000\": 0.878,\n            \"d005\": 0.88,\n            \"d025\": 0.886,\n            \"d050\": 0.891,\n            \"d100\": 0.898\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"d000\": 0.782,\n            \"d005\": 0.789,\n            \"d025\": 0.795,\n            \"d050\": 0.806,\n            \"d100\": 0.817\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"d000\": 0.305,\n            \"d005\": 0.312,\n            \"d025\": 0.328,\n            \"d050\": 0.341,\n            \"d100\": 0.354\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B数据进一步确认worst档pattern：随着scale增大，contamination inflation趋于zero。这对 framework是existential threat——如果larger models(也是评估中最受关注的models)的contamination effect太小以至于不需要calibration，那么framework的practical relevance仅限于small models (哪里contamination反而是destructive的)。这个insight本身对reframed paper有价值—— 'contamination calibration is most needed where it's hardest(small scale=destructive effect) and least needed where it's easiest(large scale=negligible effect)'。\\n\\n\\n7B延续1.5B/3B的趋势：model capacity进一步增大使contamination的marginal effect继续缩小。 MMLU inflation仅+1.5pp(7B已经在pre-training中见过大量knowledge→SFT contamination的 incremental effect minimal)。ARC和GSM8K有slightly larger inflation(+2.0pp, +3.5pp)但仍 远小于IRT可靠检测的threshold。MMLU dose-response非单调的原因：d005的SFT额外数据量太少( ~700 items)，noise dominates signal，7B在d005可能比d000略低(SFT data distribution shift)。 S2/S4在7B依然无效(AUC~0.51-0.53)——larger models的log-likelihood distribution更smooth， Min-K++的token-level statistic更难区分contaminated items。 加入7B到IRT fitting只增加~4个data points(d000/d005/d025/d100)， 且inflation pattern consistent with existing 1.5B/3B(weak)→不改变γ estimate。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"检测信号在不同training regime下的可靠性系统评估。0.5B SFT数据已有(exp_008_signal_survival_v4)。 Worst档：signals在1.5B/3B SFT上无改善，RL-post-trained模型上进一步退化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.962,\n      \"S1_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.951,\n      \"S2_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.483,\n      \"S2_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.502,\n      \"S4_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_15B\": 0.494,\n      \"S4_sft_contaminated_auc_mean_3B\": 0.519,\n      \"S1_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.891,\n      \"S2_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.478,\n      \"S4_instruct_auc_mean\": 0.534,\n      \"S1_instruct_vs_sft_delta\": -0.071,\n      \"S1_survives_sft\": true,\n      \"S1_survives_rl_proxy\": true,\n      \"S2_survives_any\": false,\n      \"S3_survives_any\": false,\n      \"S4_survives_any\": false,\n      \"overall_signals_surviving_all_regimes\": 1,\n      \"S2_reversal_at_15B\": true,\n      \"S2_reversal_at_3B\": true,\n      \"S2_reversal_cohens_d_range\": \"[-2.67, -1.22]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal × Regime × Scale AUC Heatmap Data\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.504,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.508,\n            \"3B\": 0.512\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.979,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.962,\n            \"3B\": 0.951\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S1\",\n            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.882,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.895,\n            \"3B\": 0.897\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.501,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.498,\n            \"3B\": 0.503\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.465,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.483,\n            \"3B\": 0.502\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S2\",\n            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.472,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.481,\n            \"3B\": 0.482\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-clean\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.498,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.502,\n            \"3B\": 0.505\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n            \"regime\": \"SFT-contam (d005)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.481,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.494,\n            \"3B\": 0.519\n          },\n          {\n            \"signal\": \"S4\",\n            \"regime\": \"Instruct (RL proxy)\",\n            \"0.5B\": 0.522,\n            \"1.5B\": 0.538,\n            \"3B\": 0.541\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Signal survival analysis确认worst档的核心问题：信号diversity不存在。Paper的Core Contribution #2 ('signal effectiveness characterization')的价值不在于发现'scale-dependent gradation' (这不成立)，而在于诚实记录'only embedding similarity survives across all conditions'。 Min-K++反转作为MIA cautionary tale的citation value不受影响——反而cross-scale/cross-regime 一致性使发现更robust。RL proxy下S1的~7pp AUC drop值得关注：如果RL training更aggressive (e.g., longer RL)，S1可能也会退化到<0.70threshold以下，这是未来工作的重要方向。\\n\\n\\nSFT regime的1.5B/3B结果直接继承exp-002的signal computation——scale上S2/S4保持无效。 RL proxy(Instruct models)下S1 AUC从~0.96降至~0.89：RL fine-tuning改变了model的 embedding representation space，使embedding-based similarity的train-test matching变得 less precise(但仍>0.70因为semantic similarity is relatively robust to fine-tuning)。 S2(Min-K++)在RL下更差(0.478)因为RLHF改变了token-level likelihood distribution， 进一步扰乱Min-K++的基于perplexity的detection mechanism。S4(Self-Critique)在RL下 有marginal improvement(0.534 vs 0.494-0.519)因为Instruct models更善于self-evaluation， 但仍远低于useful threshold。\\nMin-K++反转在所有scale上一致(-1.22 to -2.67 Cohen's d)，且在RL proxy下也存在—— 这是一个robust empirical finding，independent of scale and regime。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"对existing RL-trained models(Qwen2.5-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill)应用ContamCal pipeline。 Worst档：CIs极宽，expected regret分析无informative结论。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_auc_qwen_instruct_mean\": 0.891,\n      \"S1_auc_deepseek_r1_distill_mean\": 0.862,\n      \"S2_auc_rl_models_mean\": 0.479,\n      \"S4_auc_rl_models_mean\": 0.536,\n      \"rl_gamma_posterior_mean\": 0.08,\n      \"rl_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.31, 0.48]\",\n      \"rl_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"rl_95ci_coverage\": 68,\n      \"rl_ci_width_mean_pp\": 24.8,\n      \"top5_uncalibrated_vs_calibrated_rank_changes\": 0,\n      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated_pp\": 2.1,\n      \"expected_regret_calibrated_pp\": 2.4,\n      \"expected_regret_remove_rescore_pp\": 1.8,\n      \"regret_conclusion\": \"calibration does not reduce expected regret; CIs too wide to be actionable\",\n      \"known_clean_gamma_mean\": 0.04,\n      \"known_clean_gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.18, 0.27]\",\n      \"known_clean_gamma_near_zero\": true,\n      \"specificity_passes\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RL Models Calibration Summary\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.882,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.12,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.25, 0.51]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 26.3\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.895,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.07,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.28, 0.43]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 23.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.897,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.05,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.32, 0.41]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 24.1\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.901,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.03,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.29, 0.35]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 22.4\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.858,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.14,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.34, 0.62]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 28.1\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n            \"S1_auc\": 0.866,\n            \"gamma_mean\": 0.09,\n            \"gamma_ci\": \"[-0.30, 0.49]\",\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 25.7\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Expected Regret Comparison (top-5 model selection)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Uncalibrated\",\n            \"regret_pp\": 2.1,\n            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"4PL+γ calibrated\",\n            \"regret_pp\": 2.4,\n            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n            \"regret_pp\": 1.8,\n            \"rank_changes_vs_oracle\": 0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RL observational study确认worst档预期：calibration在RL regime下uninformative。 但specificity check(clean benchmark γ≈0)至少表明框架不会produce harmful false positives。 论文中frame为'current signal quality insufficient for RL models, but framework correctly expresses this uncertainty through wide CIs'——honest UQ rather than overconfident wrong answers。DeepSeek-R1-Distill的S1 AUC更低(0.86 vs 0.89)可能因为distillation 进一步distorted embedding space。这motivates future work on RL-robust signals。\\n\\n\\nRL models的observational study面临三重困难：(1)没有ground truth clean scores——无法计算 MAE，只能做internal consistency checks和regret analysis；(2)signal quality进一步降低—— S1在RL models上AUC=0.86-0.89(vs SFT的0.95+)，因为RL改变了embedding space； (3)N_models更少——仅6-8个models(不同scale的Instruct和R1-Distill variants)。\\n这三个问题叠加导致γ posterior极宽(CI=[-0.31, 0.48])，无法区分\\\"有contamination\\\"和 \\\"无contamination\\\"。Expected regret analysis显示calibrated ranking与uncalibrated ranking 几乎相同(0 rank changes in top-5)——不是因为calibration做得好，而是因为CIs太宽， calibrated scores本质上是uncalibrated scores加了大量noise。 Remove-and-rescore的regret反而最低(1.8pp)因为它简单地丢弃flagged items，不需要估计γ。\\nSpecificity check passes(known-clean benchmark的γ≈0)——这是一个small positive， 表明模型不会在clean data上hallucinate contamination effect。但这只说明false positive rate低，不说明true positive rate高。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational分析。Worst档：无ground truth，CIs宽， 结论完全inconclusive。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_auc_72B\": 0.938,\n      \"S2_auc_72B\": 0.508,\n      \"S4_auc_72B\": 0.542,\n      \"gamma_mean\": 0.02,\n      \"gamma_95ci\": \"[-0.41, 0.45]\",\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"ci_width_pp\": 28.5,\n      \"calibrated_vs_raw_delta_pp\": 0.4,\n      \"note\": \"Single model, no ground truth — purely qualitative\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"72B Observational Summary (inference only)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"raw_acc\": 0.831,\n            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.827,\n            \"delta_pp\": -0.4,\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 27.1\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n            \"raw_acc\": 0.941,\n            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.938,\n            \"delta_pp\": -0.3,\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 22.8\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"raw_acc\": 0.892,\n            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.885,\n            \"delta_pp\": -0.7,\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 31.4\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"raw_acc\": 0.793,\n            \"calibrated_acc\": 0.788,\n            \"delta_pp\": -0.5,\n            \"ci_width_pp\": 32.8\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"72B分析在worst档下几乎无信息价值。唯一可用的finding是exposure score分布的descriptive statistics——哪些benchmark items在72B上有高S1 exposure scores。但这只是signal characterization， 不是calibration。论文中作为1-2段discussion item处理，frame为'ecological validity extension requires multi-model observational study design'。不在main results中占位。\\n\\n\\n72B的observational analysis面临最严峻的identifiability challenge：(1)单个model→N_models=1， IRT无法fit(需要至少~20 models)。只能做per-item exposure scoring和descriptive analysis。 (2)无ground truth→MAE不可计算。(3)72B在所有benchmark上accuracy已接近ceiling(MMLU~0.83, ARC~0.94)→即使有contamination，其marginal inflation effect更小(ceiling compression)。 γ estimate来自在controlled models上fitted model的extrapolation到72B—— 但72B的θ远超training range，extrapolation unreliable。CI width=28.5pp使结果 完全uninformative。Calibrated score与raw score差距仅0.4pp，在noise中不可检测。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"仅ConStat + Self-Critique(无logits/embeddings)的degraded 2-signal mode。 Worst档：两个信号都在chance水平→closed-weight calibration完全不可行。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"constat_auc_mean_across_scales\": 0.524,\n      \"selfcritique_auc_mean_across_scales\": 0.511,\n      \"rrf_2signal_auc_mean\": 0.521,\n      \"mae_2signal_vs_4signal_gap_pp\": 5.8,\n      \"mae_2signal_calibration_pp\": 13.7,\n      \"mae_raw_pp\": 6.5,\n      \"note\": \"2-signal calibration WORSE than doing nothing (raw scores)\",\n      \"coverage_2signal_95pct\": 58,\n      \"ci_width_2signal_pp\": 32.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Calibration Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Exposure AUC\",\n            \"4-signal\": 0.958,\n            \"2-signal\": 0.521,\n            \"S1-only\": 0.964\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"MAE (pp)\",\n            \"4-signal\": 7.9,\n            \"2-signal\": 13.7,\n            \"S1-only\": 7.5\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"95% Coverage\",\n            \"4-signal\": 75,\n            \"2-signal\": 58,\n            \"S1-only\": 76\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"CI Width (pp)\",\n            \"4-signal\": 21.2,\n            \"2-signal\": 32.4,\n            \"S1-only\": 20.8\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Closed-weight calibration不可行是worst档下的strong negative result。论文中不应隐瞒—— 在Limitations中明确指出'ContamCal requires embedding access(open-weight models)'。 这限制了framework的practical applicability到open-weight models only。在reframed paper中， 这成为'identifiability boundary'的另一个dimension：不仅需要AUC≥0.70和N≥30， 还需要embedding access。\\n\\n\\nConStat(AUC~0.52)和Self-Critique(AUC~0.51)都接近random chance。两个random signals的 RRF fusion仍然是random(AUC=0.521)。基于这种noise exposure score做IRT calibration 不仅不帮助，还actively harmful——γ估计受random exposure scores驱动，产生spurious corrections，MAE=13.7pp远高于raw scores(6.5pp)。Coverage仅58%(95% nominal)因为 CI既宽(32.4pp)又biased(wrong γ direction on some models)。\\n这个结果有clear practical implication：closed-weight model evaluation(GPT-4, Claude等) 目前不可能做contamination calibration，因为available signals(无logits)完全无效。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.2-1B或Pythia-1.4B在3个dosage levels的controlled SFT injection。 Worst档：cross-family contamination response pattern截然不同，γ estimates不transferable。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_mmlu_d000\": 0.312,\n      \"llama_mmlu_d100\": 0.285,\n      \"llama_mmlu_inflation_pp\": -2.7,\n      \"llama_arc_d000\": 0.398,\n      \"llama_arc_d100\": 0.361,\n      \"llama_arc_inflation_pp\": -3.7,\n      \"llama_gsm8k_d000\": 0.182,\n      \"llama_gsm8k_d100\": 0.201,\n      \"llama_gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 1.9,\n      \"gamma_cross_family_correlation\": 0.31,\n      \"gamma_qwen_mmlu\": 0.018,\n      \"gamma_llama_mmlu\": -0.085,\n      \"gamma_agreement_direction\": false,\n      \"S1_llama_auc_d005\": 0.941,\n      \"S2_llama_auc_d005\": 0.472,\n      \"S4_llama_auc_d005\": 0.488\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-family Contamination Effect Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-0.5B\",\n            \"MMLU_delta\": -16.5,\n            \"ARC_delta\": -17.5,\n            \"GSM8K_delta\": -0.4\n          },\n          {\n            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-1.5B\",\n            \"MMLU_delta\": 0.8,\n            \"ARC_delta\": -0.3,\n            \"GSM8K_delta\": -0.5\n          },\n          {\n            \"family\": \"Qwen2.5-3B\",\n            \"MMLU_delta\": 0.8,\n            \"ARC_delta\": 1.2,\n            \"GSM8K_delta\": 57.7\n          },\n          {\n            \"family\": \"Llama-3.2-1B\",\n            \"MMLU_delta\": -2.7,\n            \"ARC_delta\": -3.7,\n            \"GSM8K_delta\": 1.9\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-family γ Estimates\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"qwen_gamma\": 0.018,\n            \"llama_gamma\": -0.085,\n            \"correlation\": 0.31\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"ARC\",\n            \"qwen_gamma\": -0.032,\n            \"llama_gamma\": -0.112,\n            \"correlation\": 0.58\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"qwen_gamma\": 0.31,\n            \"llama_gamma\": 0.065,\n            \"correlation\": 0.22\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-family validation失败是worst档的predicted outcome但也是valuable negative result。 它证明contamination effect is NOT a benchmark property——it's a benchmark × model family interaction。这从根本上限制了framework的generalizability：在Qwen上trained的γ estimates 不能transfer到Llama/Pythia。论文需要在Limitations中明确说明'current framework requires per-family calibration'。\\n对reframed paper的影响：(1) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity的cross-family r=0.91 claim 完全放弃；(2)Identifiability分析需要增加'family-specific'维度——每个model family都需要 独立的N≥30和AUC≥0.70；(3)作为rebuttal experiment的价值反而增加——诚实报告cross-family failure比假装成功更有说服力。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B(~1B parameters)在contamination response上类似Qwen2.5-0.5B而非1.5B—— 因为absolute model capacity而非parameter count决定contamination effect direction。 1B-class models普遍suffer from catastrophic forgetting when SFT data includes benchmark items (SFT data分布偏移干扰模型原有knowledge)。MMLU和ARC都出现deflation(-2.7pp, -3.7pp)， 与Qwen2.5-0.5B的pattern一致。\\nCross-family γ correlation仅0.31(远低于paper_framing中期望的r=0.91)——这直接否定了 'contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property'的claim。γ differences across families reflect不同的architecture/pretraining data/tokenizer导致的不同contamination response patterns。 Qwen和Llama在同一benchmark上甚至γ方向都不一致(Qwen MMLU γ>0 vs Llama MMLU γ<0)。\\nS1 AUC在Llama上依然高(0.941)——embedding similarity是model-agnostic的。S2/S4继续失败。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep_v2_final\",\n    \"description\": \"144-condition simulation sweep的最终结果(v2 currently RUNNING, 48/120 complete)。 Worst档下模拟在idealized conditions下works，但gap to real data conditions不可弥合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.04,\n      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.013,\n      \"auc080_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.018,\n      \"auc080_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.008,\n      \"structural_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.55,\n      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.7,\n      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_n\": 50,\n      \"sim_95ci_coverage_auc080_n50\": 94,\n      \"sim_95ci_coverage_auc055_n20\": 82,\n      \"fisher_info_gamma_theoretical\": \"I(γ) ∝ N × (AUC - 0.5)² / σ²_exposure\",\n      \"fisher_info_minimum_auc_for_10pct_precision\": 0.72,\n      \"real_data_effective_auc\": 0.96,\n      \"real_data_effective_n\": 26,\n      \"real_data_sim_predicted_rmse\": 0.012,\n      \"real_data_actual_rmse\": \">0.15\",\n      \"sim_to_real_gap_factor\": \">12×\",\n      \"gap_explanation\": \"simulation assumes correct model spec + local independence; real data violates both\",\n      \"sbc_at_n26_sim\": \"pass (p=0.34)\",\n      \"sbc_at_n26_real\": \"fail (p=0.003)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Simulation γ Recovery (RMSE) by AUC × N_models\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.55,\n            \"N_20\": 0.04,\n            \"N_50\": 0.026,\n            \"N_100\": 0.013,\n            \"N_200\": 0.007\n          },\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.6,\n            \"N_20\": 0.038,\n            \"N_50\": 0.023,\n            \"N_100\": 0.011,\n            \"N_200\": 0.006\n          },\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.65,\n            \"N_20\": 0.036,\n            \"N_50\": 0.021,\n            \"N_100\": 0.01,\n            \"N_200\": 0.005\n          },\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.7,\n            \"N_20\": 0.034,\n            \"N_50\": 0.019,\n            \"N_100\": 0.009,\n            \"N_200\": 0.005\n          },\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.8,\n            \"N_20\": 0.035,\n            \"N_50\": 0.018,\n            \"N_100\": 0.008,\n            \"N_200\": 0.004\n          },\n          {\n            \"AUC\": 0.9,\n            \"N_20\": 0.033,\n            \"N_50\": 0.017,\n            \"N_100\": 0.008,\n            \"N_200\": 0.004\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Sim-to-Real Gap\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"AUC=0.96 N=26\",\n            \"sim_rmse\": 0.012,\n            \"real_rmse\": \">0.15\",\n            \"gap\": \">12×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"SBC p-value\",\n            \"sim\": 0.34,\n            \"real\": 0.003,\n            \"interpretation\": \"model correctly specified in sim, misspecified in real\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Identifiability分析是worst档下仍然valuable的独立贡献——它gives理论lower bounds。 但必须诚实报告sim-to-real gap：'simulation establishes necessary conditions(AUC≥0.55 structural, ≥0.70 practical), but these are NOT sufficient conditions in real data where model assumptions are violated'。这naturally leads to future work：(1)hierarchical IRT accounting for scale-dependent effects, (2)N_models >> 50 to overcome local independence violation, (3)multiple model families for robust estimation。\\nFisher Info derivation作为appendix material仍然有theory贡献：明确了I(γ)与AUC、N、σ_e 的关系，为未来工作提供了quantitative design criteria。\\n\\n\\nSimulation sweep在idealized conditions下展示出令人鼓舞的结果——即使AUC=0.55(near chance)， γ也structurally identifiable(RMSE=0.04 at N=20)。这本身是一个有价值的理论贡献。 但worst档的核心问题是sim-to-real gap：simulation中(1)model specification完全正确 (data generating process = fitted model)，(2)local independence holds(每个examinee 独立)，(3)exposure scores按exact AUC level生成(no distribution mismatch)。\\nReal data违反所有三个假设：(1)contamination effect is scale-dependent(model misspecified)， (2)single model responds to all items(local independence violated)，(3)exposure AUC=0.96但 inflation near-zero(high AUC doesn't help when there's nothing to calibrate)。 因此simulation RMSE=0.012预测的精度在real data上inflated 12×以上。\\nFisher Information analysis gives I(γ) ∝ N × (AUC-0.5)² / σ²_e。在real conditions， AUC=0.96 gives (0.96-0.5)²=0.2116——似乎足够。但这个公式假设γ的true effect is non-zero 且model correctly specified。当true γ≈0(1.5B/3B MMLU/ARC)，Fisher Info对precision 的保证变成\\\"we can precisely estimate that γ≈0\\\"——which is correct but useless for calibration。\\nSBC通过simulation(p=0.34)但fail on real data(p=0.003)——quantitative evidence for sim-to-real gap。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis_v3_final\",\n    \"description\": \"Measurement error model(exposure as noisy observation of latent τ)的最终结果。 v1和v2已failed。Worst档：ME model收敛但不改善coverage，noise propagation正确但insufficient to compensate for model misspecification。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"me_model_converges\": true,\n      \"me_rhat_max\": 1.04,\n      \"me_ess_min\": 312,\n      \"point_estimate_95ci_coverage\": 75,\n      \"me_model_95ci_coverage\": 79,\n      \"me_coverage_improvement_pp\": 4,\n      \"target_coverage\": 95,\n      \"coverage_gap_remaining\": 16,\n      \"me_ci_width_mean_pp\": 23.8,\n      \"point_estimate_ci_width_pp\": 21.2,\n      \"me_ci_widening_pp\": 2.6,\n      \"me_mae_pp\": 7.3,\n      \"point_estimate_mae_pp\": 7.9,\n      \"me_mae_improvement_pp\": 0.6,\n      \"noise_1x_ci_widening_pct\": 8,\n      \"noise_1_5x_ci_widening_pct\": 15,\n      \"noise_2x_ci_widening_pct\": 28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Measurement Error Model vs Point-Estimate Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"MAE (pp)\",\n            \"point_estimate\": 7.9,\n            \"ME_model\": 7.3,\n            \"delta\": -0.6\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"95% Coverage (%)\",\n            \"point_estimate\": 75,\n            \"ME_model\": 79,\n            \"delta\": 4\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"95% CI Width (pp)\",\n            \"point_estimate\": 21.2,\n            \"ME_model\": 23.8,\n            \"delta\": 2.6\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Kendall τ\",\n            \"point_estimate\": 0.69,\n            \"ME_model\": 0.7,\n            \"delta\": 0.01\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Rhat max\",\n            \"point_estimate\": 1.12,\n            \"ME_model\": 1.04,\n            \"delta\": -0.08\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ME model是worst档下的minor positive：它technically works but doesn't solve the core problem。 论文中作为ablation报告：'measurement error model improves convergence(Rhat 1.12→1.04) and modestly improves coverage(75%→79%), but the dominant coverage gap source is local independence violation which requires structural model changes(e.g., hierarchical IRT or random-effects item parameters), not exposure noise propagation。' 这strengthens identifiability分析的narrative——even with proper noise handling， fundamental model limitations remain。\\n\\nME model在技术上works：它correctly propagates exposure uncertainty into posterior， 产生slightly wider CIs(+2.6pp)和slightly better coverage(+4pp)。但coverage improvement from 75%→79%远不足以close 20pp gap to 95% nominal。原因：exposure measurement error 只是coverage gap的minor contributor(~15% per SBC attribution)。主要原因是local independence violation(~60%)和model misspecification(~25%)——ME model不address these。\\nPost-hoc noise injection实验shows CI widening scales linearly with noise level (as expected from theory)——这validates the ME model mechanics。但即使at 2× noise， CIs only widen 28%，coverage仅reaches ~83%——still below 95%。\\nME model作为D025 framing中的'if improves coverage → report; otherwise → ablation' decision node：in worst tier, it's an ablation item. Simple model(point-estimate exposure) is primary because ME model adds complexity without closing the coverage gap。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1033,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1033}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DDZZ7HJdXpP3fEfCrMUzjn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me write the full LaTeX paper. This is a \"worst\" tier dream paper, meaning the core framework claims don't hold up well. The narrative guidance says to reframe as \"When Can We Calibrate Contaminated Benchmarks?\" with identifiability analysis and signal characterization as core contributions, and calibration framework as an informative negative result.\n\nLet me organize the paper structure:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Related Work\n4. Method (ContamCal framework)\n5. Experiments\n   - Signal effectiveness (stage1_signal_pipeline)\n   - RRF aggregation (rrf_aggregation_ablation)\n   - IRT calibration and baselines (irt_calibration_and_baselines)\n   - Scale bridging 7B (scale_bridging_7b)\n   - Signal survival analysis (signal_survival_analysis)\n   - RL observational case study (rl_observational_case_study)\n   - 72B observational (observational_72b)\n   - Closed-weight 2-signal mode (closed_weight_2signal_mode)\n   - Multi-family validation (multi_family_validation)\n   - Simulation identifiability sweep (simulation_identifiability_sweep_v2_final)\n   - Noise propagation analysis (noise_propagation_analysis_v3_final)\n\nNow I'm planning out the paper structure with dedicated sections for each experiment. I have 11 experiments total, so I'll need to organize them carefully with individual tables and results for each one. The core sections will cover the methodology—contamination signal detection, IRT calibration with contamination augmentation, and Fisher information analysis—followed by experiments grouped by theme: signal effectiveness, aggregation methods, calibration results, and scaling approaches.\n\nThen I'll add sections for signal robustness across different training conditions, observational studies with reinforcement learning, closed-weight model analysis, cross-family validation, simulation identifiability, and measurement error modeling. I'll consolidate some of these as subsections to keep the paper manageable, then start writing the LaTeX document using a standard article class.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5316,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20640,"cache_read_input_tokens":23164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20640},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07012785-3c12-4d16-81cb-36dc4e6c7306","uuid":"63136dbe-dc26-4968-bbd9-8f0d7b6ad6a2"}
